ket leader in gripping technology, we combine a decade of robotic-hand expertise and real industrial access with the speed and ambition of a deep-tech startup.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn't a research project waiting for its first customer. We already have a product, customers are ready to use it, and we are launching now. Your work will directly shape the electronics, actuators, and embedded systems that make that possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join at the moment when the hard engineering questions become real product decisions: how do we make a highly capable robotic hand reliable, manufacturable, serviceable, and simple enough to deploy on a real shop floor?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Sensor Engineer (Tactile &amp; Proprioception) at TACTILIA Robotics, you will build the neural architecture of physical touch and spatial awareness that gives our robotic hands human-like dexterity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own the complete sensing architecture—from evaluating tactile technologies and proprioceptive layouts to designing readout electronics, calibration matrix algorithms, and real-time sensor pipelines.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fitting high-density sensing skins, force feedback, and position tracking into a tight hand envelope means balancing signal integrity, low latency, and mechanical durability under high cyclic wear. You will work closely with Mechanics, Electronics, and Software to turn raw physical contact into clean, reliable data for real-time robotic control.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will do:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the sensing architecture.</strong> Lead the evaluation, selection, and overall design of tactile and proprioceptive sensing systems across fingers, palm, and joints—built for modularity across product variants, not a one-off prototype.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Develop tactile array hardware.</strong> Design and prototype high-resolution tactile sensors (optical, capacitive, piezoresistive, or magnetic) tailored for space-constrained, contact-rich finger pads and palm surfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineer proprioceptive feedback.</strong> Implement joint- and drive-level feedback mechanisms, including high-precision position/angle sensing, strain gauge force bridges, load cells, and tendinous tension tracking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design readout electronics &amp; AFEs.</strong> Build low-noise analog front-ends (AFEs), signal conditioning circuits, and local readout hardware optimized for minimal latency, wide dynamic range, and high immunity to electromagnetic interference (EMI).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build calibration &amp; processing pipelines. </strong>Implement automated calibration protocols, thermal/drift compensation matrix algorithms, and feature extraction (e.g., slip detection, contact point estimation) to feed clean telemetry to the software stack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Characterize &amp; validate on real hardware.</strong> Own sensor testing on custom rigs—evaluating dynamic response, force linearity, hysteresis, spatial resolution, and long-term mechanical wear over hundreds of thousands of cycles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive sensor manufacturing &amp; yield. </strong>Partner with specialized suppliers on Design for Manufacturing (DFM) for flexible/rigid-flex PCBs, molded tactile skins, and elastomeric components, ensuring high assembly yield and second-sourcing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work across the whole team.</strong> Tight loop with Mechanics (for load paths and physical packaging), Electronics (for board interfaces), and Software (for state estimation and closed-loop grasp control).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, Physics, Sensorics, Robotics, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5–10 years of experience developing sensor hardware, mechatronic instrumentation, or sensor fusion systems, including at least one product taken into series production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep domain expertise in tactile sensing modalities (e.g., optical tactile/GelSight style, piezoresistive, capacitive) or high-density proprioceptive feedback (encoders, strain gauges, load cells).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in analog circuit design, signal conditioning (AFE), active filtering, and high-SNR data acquisition for physical sensors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with sensor calibration techniques, thermal/hysteresis modeling, signal processing, and standard communication buses (SPI, I2C, CAN).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience designing or integrating flexible PCBs, molded elastomers, or miniaturized mechatronic assemblies into tight physical envelopes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong hardware mindset: you enjoy lab bring-up, sensor characterization on test rigs, and tracing physics-to-signal anomalies with scopes and logic analyzers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English; German is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Bonus:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in real-time embedded C/C++ firmware or ROS/ROS2 for sensor data processing and filtering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with tactile algorithms for slip prediction, texture recognition, or contact shape estimation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with soft robotics, stretchable electronics, or conductive polymers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of Machinery Regulation, ISO/TS 15066, and sensor design for collaborative applications.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">The next chapter of robotics won't be built in a lab. It will be built by people who care about what happens when technology meets the real world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At TACTILIA, you'll work on one of the hardest open problems in robotics: giving machines the dexterity, reliability, and robustness they need to interact with the physical world at industrial scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The technology is taking shape. The team is being built. And the standards for robotic hands and their skills are still wide open.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That means your decisions will have a lasting impact — not just on a product, but on what comes next for Physical AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the hand. Define the standard. Shape what comes next.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited by the challenge of building robotic hands that work reliably in the real world, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/tactiliarobotics/senior-sensor-engineer-munich-74723","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1794476428},{"slug":"qa-engineer-hamburg-18682","company_name":"adjoe","title":"QA Engineer (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">adjoe builds the technologies behind mobile apps growth and monetization. With our core product <strong>Playtime Arcade</strong>, we've become the global leader in rewarded advertising, an ad unit built on a simple premise: users earn real in-app rewards for engaging with new apps. The result is one of the most effective value exchanges in adtech, connecting advertisers and publishers with over 770 million users annually.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transforming 50M+ daily events into real-time actionable dashboard insights</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Dashboards team is responsible for the systems and interfaces that define our partners' daily operations. We build the campaign management APIs, analytics engines, and high-throughput tools that allow advertisers and publishers to configure, monitor, and optimize their activity on our platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not about simple CRUD interfaces, it is about building high-performance data surfaces that drive massive business decisions. Using <strong>Go, Kafka,</strong> and<strong> Druid, </strong>we process and render real-time analytics across <strong>50+ million daily events,</strong> ensuring accuracy and complex campaign performance reporting at scale. On the frontend, we tackle genuine engineering constraints: utilizing <strong>TypeScript </strong>and<strong> React,</strong> we have moved beyond standard library limitations to build highly optimized graph-rendering with <strong>Recharts </strong>capable of visualizing datasets that would overload conventional solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Mission &amp; Who We Are Looking For:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>QA with 3 years+ hands on automation experience, alongside a strong manual testing foundation.</strong> You design and execute structured and exploratory test cases, validate complex user journeys across frontend and backend, and perform regression testing before releases. You identify edge cases and risk areas early and document clear, reproducible bug reports in <strong>Jira</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You contribute to UI and API test automation using<strong> Playwright</strong>, identify critical regression flows worth automating, and maintain existing test suites. CI/CD integration experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>API and data testing is part of your toolkit.</strong> You test APIs and data-driven dashboard features, and have basic SQL knowledge for backend data validation. You understand what correct looks like at the data layer, not just the UI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality ownership from day one.</strong> You participate in refinement and sprint planning from a QA perspective, help define acceptance criteria and test strategies, and proactively flag quality risks before they reach release.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Plus:</strong> Experience in SaaS, AdTech, or performance marketing environments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌎 We welcome applications from talent worldwide and provide relocation support to Hamburg, Germany for those ready to join our team.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in It for You?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At adjoe, you’re not here to just close JIRA tickets, you’re helping build the infrastructure behind one of the most impactful platforms in adtech. The systems you work on will reach hundreds of millions of users and power billions of decisions every day.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go Big.</strong> Own projects with impact on 770M users and push adtech boundaries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Move Fast.</strong> Ship solutions multiple times a day, learn from results, and keep momentum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be Direct.</strong> Solve problems openly and collaborate across teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Thrive Together.</strong> Grow with a diverse, global team of people from over 40 different countries that learn from each other. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Have Fun.</strong> Celebrate wins, enjoy daily victories, and bring your energy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We welcome applications from people who will contribute to the diversity of our company.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/adjoe/qa-engineer-hamburg-18682","tags":["adjoe"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hamburg","created_at":1794476427},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-net-ecosystem-berlin-109033","company_name":"Clickhouse","title":"Senior Software Engineer (.NET Ecosystem)","description":"<h2><strong>About the team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Integrations Ecosystem org builds the drivers, SDKs, connectors and BI integrations that make ClickHouse feel native in any stack. The Language Clients team maintains the official clients for Python, JavaScript, Java, Go, Rust, C++ and C#, plus the ODBC, JDBC and ADBC drivers. We're small, senior and remote across North America and EMEA. Each client has a primary owner, but no client belongs to one person: we review and co-maintain across languages and decide cross-client questions together.</p><h2><strong>The role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a product-minded engineer to own the ClickHouse .NET client. You'll decide what the client should do by talking to the developers who use it, reading the issues and the telemetry, and listening to the community. Then you'll build it, with deep .NET expertise, and measure whether it worked. Your scope is the SDK and what builds on it: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://ADO.NET">ADO.NET</a>, Dapper and Entity Framework Core users, and the tools and integrations that depend on your client.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Know who uses the client and what they're trying to do. Define what good looks like (time to first query, error clarity, adoption by key integrations), measure it, and let that drive the roadmap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the voice of ClickHouse for .NET developers. Speak at .NET conferences and meet-ups, and write the posts, tutorials and samples that developers and AI assistants find when they search for how to use ClickHouse from .NET (SEO and GEO). Answer questions where the community asks them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the .NET client and its ecosystem: the client, the EF Core provider and ORM integrations, NuGet releases and support. Evolve it without breaking the people who depend on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review and co-maintain other clients, and take part in cross-client decisions on types, errors and protocol features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring what .NET and Windows users need to the ODBC driver, since that's how many Windows and BI tools reach ClickHouse. If you write C++, contribute to it directly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring written proposals about where we invest next. You set direction rather than wait for it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make the client enterprise-ready: TLS and certificate handling, authentication including Microsoft Entra ID, safe credential handling, signed and reproducible packages, and the audit and compliance questions large .NET shops ask before they adopt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the client for agents as users: an API, docs and error messages an AI coding agent can use correctly on the first try.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extend our AI development platform, with new workflows for maintaining the clients: consistency checks across languages, issue triage, release checks.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About you</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product-minded. You decide what to build from user evidence, measure whether it worked, and can explain what you chose not to build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in software, much of it on data-intensive systems: drivers, SDKs, data access, ingestion or analytics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep C# and .NET expertise: memory management, async and the TPL, Span and pooling, profiling and benchmarking. You reason about throughput and latency down to allocations and bytes on the wire, and you prove it with tests and benchmarks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in C#, and productive in at least one more of our client languages (Python, JavaScript, Java, Go, Rust, C++). You'll review and co-own across clients, not only .NET.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built or substantially extended a library other engineers depend on, and shipped NuGet packages across .NET Framework and modern .NET. You treat breaking changes accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in .NET data access (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://ADO.NET">ADO.NET</a>, Dapper, EF Core) and at home in the wider .NET ecosystem: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://ASP.NET">ASP.NET</a> Core, Aspire, NuGet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Security-minded. You've shipped a library into enterprise environments and know what security, compliance and procurement teams look for in a dependency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enthusiastic about working in public. You've given talks or written technical content, or you're keen to, and you see it as part of the job rather than a distraction from it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thoughtful use of AI development tools, with the judgment to review what comes out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear writing. Most coordination happens in design docs, PRs and RFCs.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClickHouse, especially its type system, or another OLAP engine.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">C++ and ODBC driver internals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building or maintaining an <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://ADO.NET">ADO.NET</a> or EF Core provider.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open-source contributions to .NET or data infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing SDKs, docs or error messages with AI coding agents as the consumer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Protocol or wire-format work on a database driver or network client.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Learn more</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://clickhouse.com/blog/introducing-the-blazing-fast-native-tcp-client-for-net"><u>Introducing the (blazing fast!) native TCP client for .NET</u></a>: zero-copy columnar reads, 1.5 to 2x faster than HTTP, over 99% fewer GC allocations (Oct 2026)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://clickhouse.com/blog/whats-new-clickhouse-net-driver-10-to-13"><u>What's new in the ClickHouse .NET Driver: the road from 1.0 to 1.3</u></a> (Aug 2026)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://clickhouse.com/blog/meet-groeneai-our-autonomous-contributor-to-clickhouse"><u>Meet GroeneAI: our autonomous contributor to ClickHouse</u></a> (Oct 2026)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://clickhouse.com/blog/dotnet-api-gateway-aspire"><u>Building a .NET API Gateway with ClickHouse and Aspire</u></a> (Jun 2026)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://github.com/ClickHouse/clickhouse-cs"><u>The .NET client on GitHub</u></a> and its <a target="_blank" rel