'll coordinate the specialists, keep work moving between teams and make sure every deliverable meets the quality and regulatory standard. That frees our domain teams to get back to their own work.</p><p><strong>What you'll own</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Usability studies:</strong> You'll own the study calendar, protocols and relationships with external labs such as Sage Research. This covers formative and summative studies across hardware and software, including FDA submission work for Hilo Medical. You'll make sure findings get back to design on a regular schedule.</li><li><strong>IFU and Quick Start Guide:</strong> You'll decide what content goes in the QSG, the app and the IFU. You'll also own version control and localisation (Phrase, Novalins) and brief and manage freelance designers and print partners.</li><li><strong>Packaging:</strong> You'll own packaging briefs from start to finish and coordinate agencies (ARD, Superhuit, Carac Design) and freelance packaging designers. You'll keep the work aligned with regulatory, cost and manufacturing constraints.</li><li><strong>Clinical studies:</strong> You'll connect the human factors evidence from ClinOps-run trials with the human factors evidence for the product we ship to customers.</li><li><strong>Roadmap and reporting:</strong> You'll keep a single human factors roadmap and manage dependencies, resourcing and budgets across teams. Each month you'll report confidence levels and raise any risks to leadership.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>This is a part time contractor role of up to three days per week, with a total fee of CHF 17,500 for the initial engagement. We would like to start as soon as possible, with a review after three months.</strong></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul><li>Human factors or usability engineering experience in medical devices, ideally with wearables or connected health</li><li>Proven project or programme management: you've owned the plan, se