ur platform must scale seamlessly, without increasing developer toil.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an Engineering Manager who acts as a servant leader. You will guide a high-leverage remote team of four infrastructure engineers and drive the evolution toward a scalable zero-toil platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the organizational level, you will ensure that the right way is the easy way, serving as an advocate for the engineers who rely on the platform every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re excited about building autonomous, high-leverage platform teams at scale, we’d love to talk!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Ensure we continuously deliver and improve our infrastructure platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide the team through massive reduction of manual work  through employing an AI-driven engineering approach. You will reach a zero-touch scalable infrastructure, where AI handles dependency management, assists with incident resolution, cloud cost optimization, and developer support - ensuring the team can handle increasing scope and scale without having to grow in size.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Quality surge: You will prepare, define and ensure execution of the strategy for our CI/CD and artifact distribution systems to scale without increasing engineering toil</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow, mentor and coach a high-leverage platform team of 4 Infrastructure engineers, by setting clear expectations, giving actionable and timely feedback, and fostering a culture of empathy, autonomy, and continuous improvement, in an asynchronous, remote environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability and/or willingness to use <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="external-link" href="https://accounts.cloud.camunda.io/signup?_ga=2.47330343.127558761.1654184528-504024057.1654184528">our product</a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People leadership experience: track record of growing engineers to senior and beyond senior levels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder leadership: Ability to translate tech needs into actionable engineering roadmap and strategy, and implement that across teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior-level technical depth and competency: Hands-on experience with:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloud providers (e.g., GCP, AWS or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kubernetes (any distribution)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Infrastructure as Code (e.g., Terraform, ArgoCD or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scaling high-load CI/CD systems (e.g., GitHub Actions with self-hosted runners or similar).</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backend engineering background, fluent in at least one programming language (e.g. Python)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable at reviewing complex architecture and code; eager to contribute hands-on when needed (e.g. to implement internal workflow automations)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of ensuring team efficiency within remote, async-first environments</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-haves:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience transforming teams into AI-native and/or automation-first teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in technical product management or strong product thinking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience implementing FinOps practices and accountability</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong> This role is an existing vacancy</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#L