ify it for flight. This inter-disciplinary position includes hands-on work on the test benches for the Pressure Control System (PCS), the Air Recirculation System (ARS) and the Crew and Emergency systems (CES). A major part of the work is to ensure the activities are documented properly according to the ECSS development process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Key responsibilities</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your position as an ECLSS Engineer Intern, your role includes:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Verifying NASA ISS requirements applicable to ECLSS components through test and analysis data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build hands-on on test support equipments (GSEs) and functional test benches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting test activities and validating simulation results against test data for accuracy and reliability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualifying hardware components for internal designs and externally sourced parts in environmental testing such as vibration, shock and thermal cycling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicating effectively and providing recommendations through the preparation and presentation of technical data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Writing technical documentation and participating in internal and external reviews</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><h1>What we would love to see from you</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's degree in Aerospace Engineering, Engineering Science, or Mechanical Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with aerospace hardware, ideally pressure systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong background in fluid mechanics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with programming (Python) and data analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work both independently and as part of a team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Precision in ensuring compliance with ECSS processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding the implications of interacting with a crewed space station</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Systems engineering mindset</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English; German is a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong skills in organizing and prioritizing of tasks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Positive and flexible attitude to get the job done</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to communicate across all levels of the organization</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behavior consistent with The Exploration Company's core values: Commitment, Innovation, Trust, Quality, and Teamwork</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why you should join us!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes us special here at The Exploration Company and why we think you will enjoy working here is:  </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Agile - we make decisions fast whilst keeping our goals and systems in mind </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Open and Collaborative - we are transparent about risks and obstacles, so that we can cooperate to overcome them  </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have a lot of Fun - we refuel our energy knowing we are democratising space. It’s a wonderful and rare opportunity, are YOU up for the challenge?  </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd love to hear from you if you wish to be a part of our journey. Please submit your CV now for immediate consideration and we will be in touch shortly. <br /> <br /><em>The Exploration Company is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity. We do not discriminate based on race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability status. Relocation ass