 style="min-height:1.5em">Perform functional validation and qualification of avionics equipment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Move units from first prototypes to Engineering Models, Qualification Models and Flight Models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flow down and validate requirements to unit level</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your capacity as an Avionics Equipment Technical Owner, your role will be continuously evolving, but day to day your duties will include:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Point of contact and full responsible </strong>for one avionics unit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owner </strong>of the equipment from concept and breadboard phase to flight model</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owner</strong> of unit documentation, ICDs and requirements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owner </strong>of box level FDIR and FMEA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coordination of all disciplines </strong>working on a unit (electronics design engineers, mechanical design engineers, system engineers, test team, EGSE team)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coordination </strong>and run of test campaigns (EM, QM, FM) covering functional and environmental tests (vibe, shock, TVAC, EMC) with the environmental load specialists</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analysis</strong> of test data after test campaigns</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Definition of roadmap for unit improvement (between models and between flights)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Closely working with functional chains (thermal, ECLSS, Propulsion, etc.) to plan system level tests with the units embedded</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Continuous Learning:</strong> Stay current with industry trends, emergi