ing. Some roles, like sales in the US, are hybrid—please check the job description.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Giving back</strong> 🤝 – We're big fans of open source, and you'll get $100 per month to support projects you care about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transparency</strong> 🙏 – We all know what everyone’s working on, how the company is doing—the whole shebang.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>*Country and/or State specific details provided in your employment agreement.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/n8n/lead-deployment-strategist-emea-berlin-414517","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin Office","created_at":1794454817},{"slug":"head-of-enterprise-product-berlin-158161","company_name":"N8N","title":"Head of Enterprise Product","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The AI orchestration of your wildest imagination.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">n8n is the open workflow orchestration platform built for the new era of AI. We give technical teams the freedom of code with the speed of no-code, so they can automate faster, smarter, and without limits. Backed by a fiercely inventive community and 500+ builder-approved integrations, we’re changing the way people bring systems together and scale ideas for impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our founding in 2019, we’ve grown into a diverse team of over 260 - working across Europe and the US, connected by a shared builder spirit and with our centre of gravity in Berlin. Along the way, we’ve:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivated a community of more than 650,000 active developers and builders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earned 190K+ GitHub stars, making us one of the world’s Top 40 most popular projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top investors, from Sequoia’s first German seed to our SAP's recent strategic investment - bringing us to a $5.2bn valuation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />That’s the company we’ve built. Now we’d love to see what <em>you </em>can build. If you’re applying, try n8n out - whether you’re technical or not - and share a screenshot of your first workflow with us. The easiest place to start is here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://app.n8n.cloud/register"><u>app.n8n.cloud/register</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in a defining moment of an incredible journey. Come and build with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your main goal will be to <strong>lead n8n’s enterprise product strategy and build scalable monetisation infrastructure</strong>, turning complex enterprise needs into innovative, reusable capabilities while preserving the simplicity, flexibility, and product-led experience that make n8n successful.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />To make this happen, you'll take ownership of four key areas:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Shape our enterprise product vision and strategy</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and drive our enterprise product vision, translating the needs of builders, admins, and buyers across governance, security, compliance, scale, and reliability into reusable product capabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify new opportunities, make thoughtful product bets, and decide which customer requests to prioritise, decline, or transform into broader solutions rather than reacting to individual deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion exceptional product craft, usability, and quality, balancing innovation with enterprise readiness and measuring success through adoption, time-to-value, retention, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h3>Own and scale our monetisation infrastructure</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the product strategy, priorities, and roadmap for monetisation infrastructure, enabling evolving commercial models without creating unnecessary complexity, exceptions, or workarounds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Growth, Finance, Sales, and self-serve product teams to inform pricing, packaging, and tiering decisions while maintaining clear ownership of product priorities and outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make strategic trade-offs between new commercial capabilities, foundational investments, and simplification, ensuring reliable, scalable infrastructure with clear dependencies and realistic delivery commitments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Build a high-performing product function and drive technical alignment</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape and lead the enterprise Product Management function, owning team structure, hiring, performance, and career development while empowering PMs to make strong, autonomous decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Engineering leadership to build ambitious yet achievable roadmaps, making informed decisions about scope, sequencing, architectural constraints, and technical dependencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balance new product capabilities with technical debt, platform investment, and reliability, establishing clear ownership, effective prioritisation, and strong collaboration between Product and Engineering.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Be the strategic product partner to customers and commercial teams</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build deep knowledge of our enterprise customers, personally leading senior-level roadmap conversations, understanding their evolving needs, and navigating complex product escalations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted product counterpart to Sales, Customer Success, Legal/Security, and partners, translating customer and commercial insights into strategic product decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set clear expectations with commercial teams and customers, confidently challenging account-specific requests when needed and ensuring long-term product value drives prioritisation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>REQUIREMENTS</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Must-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enterprise product strategy:</strong> You have a proven track record of turning complex enterprise customer needs into scalable product capabilities, with the judgement to prioritise meaningful opportunities and confidently say no when necessary.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product-led mindset:</strong> You understand how to meet sophisticated enterprise requirements without compromising the broader product experience, and you maintain a high bar for usability, simplicity, and product craft.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Monetisation expertise:</strong> You have led monetisation infrastructure initiatives or bring a strong understanding of the systems, technical dependencies, and commercial trade-offs required to support scalable business models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial fluency:</strong> You have navigated pricing, packaging, renewals, or enterprise deal considerations and know how to balance commercial opportunities with sustainable product strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical credibility:</strong> You can confidently partner with Engineering leaders to evaluate architecture constraints, make informed prioritisation decisions, and balance innovation with 