:"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The AI orchestration of your wildest imagination.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">n8n is the open workflow orchestration platform built for the new era of AI. We give technical teams the freedom of code with the speed of no-code, so they can automate faster, smarter, and without limits. Backed by a fiercely inventive community and 500+ builder-approved integrations, we’re changing the way people bring systems together and scale ideas for impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our founding in 2019, we’ve grown into a diverse team of over 260 - working across Europe and the US, connected by a shared builder spirit and with our centre of gravity in Berlin. Along the way, we’ve:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivated a community of more than 650,000 active developers and builders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earned 190K+ GitHub stars, making us one of the world’s Top 40 most popular projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top investors, from Sequoia’s first German seed to our SAP's recent strategic investment - bringing us to a $5.2bn valuation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />That’s the company we’ve built. Now we’d love to see what <em>you </em>can build. If you’re applying, try n8n out - whether you’re technical or not - and share a screenshot of your first workflow with us. The easiest place to start is here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://app.n8n.cloud/register"><u>app.n8n.cloud/register</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in a defining moment of an incredible journey. Come and build with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎯 Your main goal will be to build and lead a high-performing regional Forward Deployed Engineering (FDE) team that accelerates enterprise customer adoption by turning high-impact automation use cases into production-ready workflows. You'll own technical delivery quality, team development, and regional execution, while staying hands-on and empowering customers to become independent, successful builders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To achieve this, you'll focus on four key areas:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Build &amp; Lead a High-Performing FDE Team</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire, onboard, and coach Forward Deployed Engineers across your region, partnering closely with Deployment Strategists to deliver high-impact customer engagements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set and maintain a high technical quality bar for production workflows, custom nodes, integration architectures, and customer-facing delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage regional team capacity, workload, and staffing while staying hands-on with customer engagements and supporting your team's technical development.</p></li></ul><h3>Own Regional Delivery &amp; Customer Outcomes</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead regional engagement intake and prioritization with Customer Success, Sales, and Partnerships, focusing resources on high-value accounts, strategic adoption opportunities, and at-risk renewals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualify and scope customer engagements, selecting the right mix of internal FDEs and delivery partners while ensuring clear success criteria, technical ownership, and timelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive measurable customer outcomes through production-ready workflows, increased adoption, and seamless handovers to Customer Success Managers, while reporting regional results and expansion signals to leadership.</p></li></ul><h3>Enable Customers &amp; Scale Technical Excellence</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion a customer-first delivery approach where customers build alongside FDEs, develop technical confidence, and become capable of maintaining and scaling their own automations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and continuously improve reusable technical assets, including workflow templates, reference architectures, workshop materials, and hackathon playbooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capture learnings from customer engagements and turn them into scalable best practices that improve delivery quality and consistency across the global FDE team.</p></li></ul><h3>Drive Partner Quality &amp; Cross-functional Collaboration</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with regional partner managers and the Partner Delivery Manager to ensure partner-led engagements meet n8n's technical and delivery standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support partner technical readiness, certification, and quality reviews to build a reliable regional ecosystem of delivery resources.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Product and Engineering to translate customer feedback, integration gaps, feature requests, and custom node needs into actionable priorities, balancing reusable product improvements with customer-specific solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>REQUIREMENTS</h2><h3><strong>Must-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🛠️ Technical Customer-Facing Experience:</strong> You have 6+ years of experience in forward deployed engineering, solutions engineering, professional services, or technical consulting within a software company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌟 Technical Leadership:</strong> You have 2+ years of experience leading and coaching technical teams, with a track record of developing talent and raising the bar for customer-facing technical delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>⚡ Automation &amp; Integration Expertise:</strong> You have hands-on experience with workflow automation, integration platforms, or low-code tools and can confidently design and troubleshoot complex automation solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🏗️ Enterprise Technical Delivery:</strong> You're experienced in building production-ready workflows and integrations, with a strong understanding of APIs, authentication, data handling, security, and enterprise architecture considerations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🤝 Cross-functional Collaboration:</strong> You're comfortable working across Sales, Customer Success, Product, Engineering, and Partnerships to align priorities, manage expectations, and make thoughtful trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🎯 Customer Outcome Mindset:</strong> You know how to balance technical excellence with business impact, identify high-value use cases, and empower customers to become self-sufficient rather than dependent on ongoing services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 Player-Coach Mentality:</strong> You enjoy staying close to the technology and customer challenges while building a high-performing team, creating repeatable processes, and scaling delivery in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌍 Regional Availability:</strong> You're based in the relevant region (EMEA or North America) and comfortable traveling to customer sites when needed.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💻 n8n Expertise:</strong> You're familiar with n8n or similar workflow automation and low-code platforms, ideally with experience building complex production workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🤝 Partner Ecosystems:</strong> You have experience working with systems integrators, technical consulting partners, or external delivery teams to deliver enterprise customer engagements.</p></li><li><p style="m