demand-generation-berlin-267053","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin Office","created_at":1794454817},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-core-platform-engine-scale-reliability-berlin-81290","company_name":"N8N","title":"Senior Product Manager - Core Platform (Engine, Scale & Reliability)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The AI orchestration of your wildest imagination.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">n8n is the open workflow orchestration platform built for the new era of AI. We give technical teams the freedom of code with the speed of no-code, so they can automate faster, smarter, and without limits. Backed by a fiercely inventive community and 500+ builder-approved integrations, we’re changing the way people bring systems together and scale ideas for impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our founding in 2019, we’ve grown into a diverse team of over 260 - working across Europe and the US, connected by a shared builder spirit and with our centre of gravity in Berlin. Along the way, we’ve:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivated a community of more than 650,000 active developers and builders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earned 190K+ GitHub stars, making us one of the world’s Top 40 most popular projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top investors, from Sequoia’s first German seed to our SAP's recent strategic investment - bringing us to a $5.2bn valuation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />That’s the company we’ve built. Now we’d love to see what <em>you </em>can build. If you’re applying, try n8n out - whether you’re technical or not - and share a screenshot of your first workflow with us. The easiest place to start is here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://app.n8n.cloud/register"><u>app.n8n.cloud/register</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in a defining moment of an incredible journey. Come and build with us.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your main goal will be to make n8n's Core Platform ready for the company's next stage of growth: more scalable, reliable, secure, and flexible as customer usage and technical complexity increase. You'll own the foundations that everything else, including our AI and agent capabilities, is built on.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">To do so, here are your responsibilities:</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>OWN THE CORE PLATFORM STRATEGY &amp; ROADMAP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and communicate the product strategy and roadmap for the Core Platform in partnership with Engineering and Product leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prioritize foundational investments based on customer impact, enterprise needs, technical risk, and engineering effort, and make trade-offs between near-term customer needs, technical debt, and long-term architecture explicit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead product discovery for technically complex problems, engaging directly with enterprise customers and internal customer-facing teams.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>SCALABILITY, RELIABILITY &amp; EXECUTION ENGINE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive work on the scalability and reliability of n8n's execution engine, including areas like worker pools and distributed execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve the reliability of triggers and execution behaviour across complex deployment setups, from multi-main Cloud environments to self-hosted enterprise installations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape a more secure and flexible approach to executing code within n8n.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>MAJOR RELEASES &amp; CROSS-ORG ALIGNMENT</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the planning and release of major or breaking platform versions, including migration strategy, stakeholder communication, and risk management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish clear success measures and keep the squad accountable for outcomes, not only delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the bridge between the Core team and the wider org: Product, Sales, Solutions Engineering, Customer Success, and Support, making platform trade-offs legible without oversimplifying them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Treat internal product teams as customers of the platform: proactively mine their roadmaps for implicit platform requirements and turn cross-cutting needs into explicit Core Platform work before they become blockers.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3>REQUIREMENTS</h3><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Must-haves</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Platform product experience:</strong> You have 5+ years in Product, with at least 2 to 3 years on platform, infrastructure, developer-facing, or backend/API products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical depth:</strong> You're credible with senior engineers. You can reason about distributed systems, execution models, and reliability/scalability trade-offs, and hold your own in an architecture discussion. You're at home with non-functional requirements, where the details are the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Complex delivery track record:</strong> You've led cross-team technical initiatives with real delivery risk, ideally including a migration or breaking change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prioritization under ambiguity:</strong> You make trade-offs explicit and connect foundational or technical-debt work to customer and commercial outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and autonomy:</strong> You grab problems without being asked, fix what you see broken, and drive outcomes without waiting for direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Exceptional communication:</strong> You make complex platform topics understandable for technical and non-technical audiences alike.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enterprise platform reality:</strong> You understand what running software in customer-controlled environments means, including self-hosted, air-gapped, and restricted deployments</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice-to-haves</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on ability:</strong> You can read code or prototype, even if you're not shipping it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enterprise exposure:</strong> You've worked with B2B SaaS requirements like security, compliance, or deployment complexity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Security partnership:</strong> You're comfortable working with security teams on code execution, isolation, or compliance topics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Domain familiarity:</strong> You know workflow automation, orchestration, or open-source / developer-community products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Writing culture:</strong> You default to writing things down to create clarity and alignment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>n8n is an equal o