urement records and collaborate with finance, operations, engineering, and quality teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help establish standardized procurement processes as purchasing activities move into a structured procurement function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the implementation of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations and ensure procurement activities follow company policies and compliance requirements.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven procurement experience in an industrial, manufacturing, engineering, aerospace, defence or similar high stakes high reliability environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing suppliers, purchasing materials or services, and supporting commercial negotiations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organizational and analytical skills, with excellent attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on, pragmatic approach to solving operational and supplier-related challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and relationship-management skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively across functions.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Desirable experience</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using an ERP system such as SAP or Microsoft Dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with procurement process improvement, ERP implementation, or structured procurement controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a high paced startup environment, building scalable processes from scratch</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Benefits and important information:</u></strong><