ght:1.5em">We’re already trusted by leading European scale-ups including Pleo, Freetrade, and Motorway. Our team is a blend of finance, product, and technical experts from top-tier companies like Uber, Plaid, Miro, Mollie, and Bunq, united by the drive to create a game-changing solution.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a team that is deeply customer-obsessed, plays to win, and isn’t afraid to take big, bold bets. We move fast, hold a high bar, and are committed to growing together as we scale.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stacks is looking for a fiercely ambitious, entrepreneurial, and commercially driven <strong>Business Development Representative / Commercial Associate</strong> to join as one of our initial GTM hires!</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this high-impact role, you’ll collaborate closely with our Sales team to create and execute our GTM strategy at Stacks. If you’re excited by the idea of limitless growth and fast-paced challenges, this is a unique opportunity to accelerate your career as you help shape the future of Stacks.</p><h2></h2><h2><strong>🧱 What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prospecting &amp; Pipeline Generation: </strong>Own outbound into Mid-Market and Enterprise companies across the UK.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Outbound Strategy: </strong>Run multi-channel campaigns across email, phone, and LinkedIn. You'll be writing, testing, and iterating constantly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Discovery &amp; Qualification: </strong>Hold sharp, insight-led conversations with finance leaders. Your consulting instincts for asking the right questions will show up here.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Mastery:</strong> Get deep on the close process fast, so you can speak credibly about debits, credits, reconciliations, and the pain of a 10-day close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional Partnership: </strong>Work directly with our Sales team to shape messaging and build a repeatable outbound motion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth Path: </strong>Clear track to AE. This is the launchpad role. You're looking at an 8-12 month trajectory into a mid-market deal-making role.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>🧩 What You Need</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Brilliant Background:</strong> 1–3 years in a top-tier environment like MBB, VC, PE or Early-stage </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical Horsepower:</strong> You think in frameworks, get to the "so what" quickly, and can break down a prospect's business in a first call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial Instinct:</strong> You want to be closer to revenue. You're motivated by tangible, measurable outcomes, not slide decks read by three people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hunger &amp; Grit:</strong> You're competitive, coachable, and don't flinch at a cold call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear Communicator: </strong>Written, spoken, and on the phone, you can be concise, direct, and persuasive.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>🚀 What’s in It for You</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Foundational role:</strong> Help shape a category-defining company from an early stage, working directly with founders and a small, high-agency team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meaningful ownership:</strong> Competitive equity in a company scaling rapidly towards $10m ARR, where your impact will directly shape the outcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cutting-edge product and tech:</strong> Work at the intersection of AI and finance, building systems that fundamentally change how companies run their financial close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-calibre team:</strong> Collaborate with people from companies like Uber, Plaid, Miro, and Mollie.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Exceptional workspace:</strong> Our London HQ is based in Fora — a modern, design-led space in the heart of the city with access to a gym, classes, and an environment built for focused, in-person building</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong team culture:</strong> We run regular socials and off-sites that bring the team together properly, we recently have our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7452732855543259136/?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAACQ1TQUB9bCcNVJHhIuwqSi-01DyuyrCVXE">2-year anniversary party</a> in Amsterdam, with board games, a tarot card reader and live music 🎶</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>🔥 Where this role can take You</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The BDR seat is the way in, not the ceiling. You'll learn the product, the persona, and the close from the front line, then move into the function that fits you best. How well you do sets how quickly you get there.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Account Executive:</strong> Own and close your own enterprise deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solutions Engineer:</strong> Run technical discovery and demo behind the close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>BD Lead:</strong> Hire and coach the next wave of BDRs as the team scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product:</strong> Shape what we build with everything you hear on the front line.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>🤝 The Hiring Process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 1:</strong> 15-minute screening call with <strong>Sam </strong>(Senior Talent Partner) to discuss your background and logistics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 2: </strong>30-minute screening call with <strong>Basile</strong> (BDR Lead) to discuss your motivation and experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 3: </strong>Take-home and 60-minute case study interview with <strong>Pepijn</strong> (BDR) to dive deeper into your commercial experience and <strong>Koen</strong> (our Founding AE) to do some role playing scenarios with you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 4: </strong>30-minute conversation with <strong>Julien</strong> (COO) to discuss growth and more!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 5: </strong>Offer!</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/stacks/commercial-associate-london-332096","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794498031},{"slug":"growth-engineer-old-street-412331","company_name":"Granola","title":"Growth Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>About Granola</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hey! We’re team Granola 👋</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building the leading AI-powered notepad for people in back-to-back meetings, a product that’s spreading through teams and redefining how knowledge is captured and used. We help teams turn messy conversations into structured insight, so they can spend more time focusing on what’s important and less time on admin.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a Growth Engineer to sit across product, data, and marketing problems - identifying opportunities, running experiments, and building product-led growth loops that feel native to the Granola experience. Our growth has been almost entirely organic. Now we want to understand it, accelerate it, and build the systems to make it compound.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full growth experimentation cycle - from spotting opportunities in the funnel to shipping, measuring, and deciding what to kill or double down on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and iterate on activation, onboarding, sharing, and retention flows that turn first-time users into daily habits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with product, marketing, and data to surface growth levers and ship improvements that compound over time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop the experimentation infrastructure (A/B testing, attribution tracking, analytics tooling), so teams can move fast and learn faster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate user behaviour and funnel data into practical product or engineering changes that improve outcomes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define success metrics before you build, evaluate impact honestly, and balance speed with strong product judgment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help shape how growth operates at Granola - the metrics that matter, the playbooks, and the bar for what good looks like</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><h3><strong>Your background looks something like…</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in growth, product, or full stack engineering, ideally with end-to-end ownership of experimentation, optimisation or conversion work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product sense and user experience, you can see problems from multiple sides and build for all of them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good understanding of metrics, success measurement and iteration</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a high-velocity startup or an environment where you've had to move fast, define your own priorities, and ship without a detailed spec</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working across the growth stack - TypeScript, React, Node.js, product analytics tools and A/B testing infrastructure</p></li></ul><h3><strong>As a person, you…</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are first and foremost a builder</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are excited to work in-person from our office in London (most of the time)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Love working in a startup environment (you either have experience working in a startup or are really drawn to the zero-to-one phase)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Value working with people who are kind, ambitious, and pragmatic</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are curious about AI, product systems, and how growth loops actually work - you enjoy digging into the mechanics of why things succeed or fail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate clearly, collaborate well across product, marketing, and engineering, and are comfortable with ambiguity in a fast-moving environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thrive in a fast-paced environment with evolving requirements and priorities</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About the Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are living in the most exciting time for tool builders since Engelbart's demo in 1968 and we want to assemble the best crew to build this future together. Our compensation philosophy is to hire the best people in the market and pay them accordingly with salary, variable, and equity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lastly, we think amazing talent comes from all kinds of life journeys and experiences. If what is written above speaks to you, whether you look like a fit on paper or not, please reach out.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/granola/growth-engineer-old-street-412331","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794498031},{"slug":"remote-compliance-security-lead-303191","company_name":"Triggerdev","title":"Compliance & Security Lead","description":"<h1>About Trigger.dev</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trigger.dev is an open source platform used by developers to build production-grade AI agents. It's an SDK and the infrastructure to run agents reliably at scale, so teams can focus on the product instead of the plumbing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Cloud product is a managed service where we deploy our users' code and auto-scale from zero to millions of executions. With the rise of AI, being able to offload async tasks reliably is a key part of any developer's toolkit: We're building the infrastructure to make that a reality.</p><h1>About the position</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for our first Compliance &amp; Security Lead to own security compliance and data protection at Trigger.dev. You'll report to the founders, and work closely with engineering.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We already hold SOC 2 Type II, run our program through Oneleet, and publish a trust portal covering SOC 2, GDPR and HIPAA. Until now the founders and engineers have handled compliance alongside their day jobs. As we grow, customers send more security questionnaires, ask for more reports and negotiate more DPAs. Now we need somebody to own this, keep it running all year, and free our engineers to build.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need to be an engineer, but technical experience is a bonus. This role suits someone process-minded who likes making compliance practical, rather than just ticking boxes.</p><h1>What you'll be doing</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll do a variety of things including:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running our SOC 2 and HIPAA programs: owning our SOC 2 audit, managing evidence collection in Oneleet and keeping us audit-ready all year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Using AI and automation to speed up compliance work, from drafting questionnaire answers to collecting evidence and reviewing policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Completing security questionnaires and vendor assessments, sharing our reports and bridge letters, and keeping our trust portal current</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reviewing and negotiating DPAs with customers and suppliers, working with our lawyers, keeping our records of processing up to date and handling data subject requests under UK and EU GDPR</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Writing and maintaining our security, privacy and data retention policies, and making sure retention periods are enforced</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reviewing new tools and sub-processors before we adopt them, and keeping our sub-processor list current</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deciding when we need new frameworks, such as ISO 27001 or ISO 42001 (the AI management standard), and leading the work to get there</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Making compliance seamless for the team: onboarding training, simple processes and automated evidence collection wherever possible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping our incident response and breach notification process ready, and testing it each year</p></li></ul><h1>Requirements</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You really need to have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in security compliance, GRC or data protection, ideally at a SaaS or developer tools company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at an early-stage startup as the first or only compliance hire, with full ownership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience running a SOC 2 audit, from evidence collection through to the final report</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An up to date working knowledge of UK and EU GDPR, and experience reviewing or negotiating DPAs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience completing security questionnaires accurately and quickly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, plain writing - you can turn a policy into something engineers will read</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enough technical understanding to talk to engineers about cloud infrastructure, access control and logging (you don't need to write code)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are remote you must be within CET to ET timezones (GMT+1:00 to GMT-5:00). We will arrange 3 in-person events throughout the year</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You'll be an amazing fit if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have experience with ISO 27001 or HIPAA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have used a compliance automation platform such as Oneleet, Vanta or Drata</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hold a privacy or security certification, such as CIPP/E, CISA or CISSP</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI tools to speed up questionnaires, evidence review and policy work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are based in the UK and able to join the team in London</p></li></ul><h1>About the team</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a small team with a flat hierarchy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We encourage continuous learning and personal development</p></l