e Remix)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A sharp eye for visual and interaction detail - typography, spacing, motion, and the small things that make software high quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working directly from a problem statement rather than a fully-specced design - you can drive design decisions yourself</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are remote you must be within CET to ET timezones (GMT+1:00 to GMT-5:00). We will arrange in-person events throughout the year</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You'll be an amazing fit if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning design end-to-end at a small startup, without a separate design team to hand off to</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Worked at a developer tools company, or have strong empathy for developers as an end user</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or evolving a design system / component library</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of shipping fast and iterating in public</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're based in the UK and you are able to join the team in London</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributed to open source projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previously been a venture-backed startup founder</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a social media presence</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About the team</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a small team with a flat hierarchy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We encourage continuous learning and personal development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everyone operates autonomously; we trust you to get the job done, but to also quickly raise your hand if you need help</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We care about our customers and the open-source community</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1