me":"Emagine","title":"Business Development Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role of Business Development Manager:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Business Development Manager for our UK team who will have responsibility for developing relationships within new logos and some existing accounts. Your focus will be on building relationships with both IT and Business decision makers in order to provide solutions and deploy project teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look for people who apply logic to their thinking, are natural self-starters, and see things through from start to finish. People who learn from every mistake are welcomed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business Development Manager - What you will be doing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business Development and account penetration will be your focus. You will be a strategic partner to Financial Services MD and C level executives, forging new relationships and selling technology and Business people/project solutions for emagine</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You, the Business Development Manager, will be responsible for mapping out cold &amp; warm accounts and developing them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You, the Business Development Manager, you will collaborate closely with our SME Consultants to provide solutions for your clients</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You, will have complete authority and ownership of the sales cycle from prospecting to close in order to exceed your quota.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business Development Manager – experience required:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business Development experience from an IT/Recruitment/ Business/Professional consulting firm</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">IT, Financial Services or Insurance consultancy or recruitment experience would be beneficial</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A creative solutions provider. Come with a solution, not a problem</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven analytical experience from a sales perspective including; forecasting, budgeting and data interpretation and analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong track record of nurturing relationships, closing business and managing processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to adopt best practices and embrace feedback. Change is welcome</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A natural leader who has the ability to work with a wide spectrum of people (from MDs to Developers) and willing to manage the whole spectrum of responsibilities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business Development Manager - What you will get in return:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent salary, competitive commission structure and an exceptional benefits package</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clearly defined career path with mapped progression and continuous training</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Management opportunities if of interest</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">To have your voice heard, influence and lead the future of the organisation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">To work in an established brand with a startup mentality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recognition programmes and sales incentives such as company trips away</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth within a diverse and global environment; opportunities to open new territories such as the US or Asia.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are up to the challenge and would like to find out more please get in touch with us immediately and apply now.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To be considered for this exciting opportunity, you will already have the legal right to live and work in the UK.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>“emagine is an equal opportunity employer, and employment practices are based strictly on merit. It is the policy of the Company to give equal opportunity in employment regardless of sex, sexual orientation, marital status, race, age, disability, gender reassignment, pregnancy and maternity, religion or ethnic origin”</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We empower companies with high-end IT services</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">emagine is a high-end business, engineering &amp; IT consulting company. Enabled by an extensive network of experts, emagine powers progress, solves challenges and delivers real results through tailored high-end consulting services. emagine is headquartered in Copenhagen, Denmark with departments in France, Germany, Ireland, the Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Sweden, United Kingdom, United Arab Emirates as well as India. Over the last couple of years, the company has grown extensively, increasing its international footprint to become one of the biggest consultancies in its segment in Europe and beyond. emagine A/S is owned by private equity company Axcel and a group of senior staff and board members.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Are you our new colleague?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At emagine, we value diversity immensely. Both when it comes to backgrounds and competences, but also in relation to personality and individual ambition. We are a diverse and well-rounded group made up of experienced specialists, generalists, recent graduates and self-taught people. We are generally curious, helpful and happy to share knowledge with our colleagues.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are proud of our values that are based on honesty, kindness, helpfulness and solidarity. We nurture a strong community culture, where cooperation is paramount – not just locally but also across borders with our international departments. Only in unison can we provide the best service to our clients and affiliated consultants – and that is our goal. As an employee of emagine, you will experience a close-knit culture in which people stand side by side and where there is an emphasis on building close relationships. Going to work must be a fun and enriching experience yet still provide a challenge. That is why we take several steps to ensure that work is motivating and engaging. Finally, we also strive to create the right conditions for physical and mental wellbeing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Want to know more about what it is like to work at emagine?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Visit our Instagram to get a better idea of who we are or get in contact with our HR department.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/emagine/business-development-manager-london-403031","tags":["Commerical Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794498030},{"slug":"global-payments-partner-lead-london-61693","company_name":"Lovable","title":"Global Payments Partner Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TL;DR: </strong>We’re looking for a Global Payments Partners Lead to co-own Lovable's global payments strategy. You’ll lead payment partnerships and work closely with Engineering, Product, and Finance to make payments seamless, improve conversion, and strengthen our payment economics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Why Lovable?</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is the software creation platform that gives people the power to act on the problems closest to them. For decades, turning an idea into software required so much capital, technical fluency, and time that many ideas never came to life. Lovable is the counterargument: a platform for all people with ideas, ambition, and problems worth solving. From solopreneurs to small business owners to teams at companies like Adidas and Zendesk, people have built over 60 million projects on Lovable since its launch in November 2024. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building a generational company from Stockholm, with growing teams in London, Boston, New York, and San Francisco. Our team is small, talent-dense, and moving quickly, with a culture rooted in extreme ownership, high velocity, and low-ego collaboration. We look for people who care deeply, ship fast, and are eager to make a dent in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is one of TIME’s 100 Most Influential Companies and has been recognized on the Forbes AI 50 and CNBC Disruptor 50, reflecting our momentum as one of Europe’s fastest-growing AI companies and one of the most ambitious places to build in this next era of software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve owned payments at scale across multiple markets, with a track record of improving acceptance, costs, and recurring payment performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in card payments, acquiring, local payment methods, and subscriptions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An exceptional negotiator with a proven track record of securing better pricing and commercial terms from payment providers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical and analytical depth, with the ability to turn payment data into clear priorities and shipped improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A senior, hands-on operator who sets direction, aligns teams, and takes responsibility for results.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set the strategy.</strong> Co-own the global payments roadmap and prioritize investments across providers, markets, and payment methods.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own &amp; Improve performance.</strong> Increase successful checkouts and renewals, recover failed payments, and reduce processing costs while managing fraud and disputes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead payment partnerships.</strong> Own provider relationships and performance reviews. Lead negotiations on pricing, contract terms, and service commitments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ship improvements.</strong> Partner with Product and Engineering on payment experiences, integrations, and migrations across subscriptions and credit purchases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build for scale.</strong> Establish reporting, monitoring, and operational processes. Work with Finance, Legal, and Security on reconciliation, compliance, and reliability.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About your application</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please submit your application in English. It’s our company language, so you’ll be speaking lots of it if you join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tell us about a payments initiative you’ve led: the problem, your contribution, and the measurable result.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We treat all candidates equally. If you’re interested, please apply through our careers portal.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lovable/global-payments-partner-lead-london-61693","tags":["EPD"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794498029},{"slug":"performance-marketer-paid-search-london-361219","company_name":"Lovable","title":"Performance Marketer, Paid Search","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TL;DR -</strong> We're looking for a hands-on paid marketer to run search and display across Google, Microsoft, The Trade Desk and emerging channels such as ChatGPT ads. You'll build agents with Lovable that read performance, move budgets, catch issues, and make changes. This is an IC role for someone senior who likes being in the detail and building the machine, not just operating it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Lovable?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is the software creation platform that gives people the power to act on the problems closest to them. For decades, turning an idea into software required so much capital, technical fluency, and time that many ideas never came to life. Lovable is the counterargument: a platform for all people with ideas, ambition, and problems worth solving. From solopreneurs to small business owners to teams at companies like Adidas and Zendesk, people have built over 60 million projects on Lovable since its launch in November 2024. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building a generational company from Stockholm, with growing teams in London, Boston, New York, and San Francisco. Our team is small, talent-dense, and moving quickly, with a culture rooted in extreme ownership, high velocity, and low-ego collaboration. We look for people who care deeply, ship fast, and are eager to make a dent in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is one of TIME’s 100 Most Influential Companies and has been recognized on the Forbes AI 50 and CNBC Disruptor 50, reflecting our momentum as one of Europe’s fastest-growing AI companies and one of the most ambitious places to build in this next era of software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>7+ years running paid search and display channels.</strong> You've owned significant budgets across Google, you know your way around Microsoft Ads, and you've worked in at least one DSP (DV360, Criteo, or The Trade Desk).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automation-led.</strong> You don't do by hand what a script or an agent could do. You've built automations for reporting, budget pacing, or optimisation, and you're comfortable with platform APIs and pulling your own data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A social-creative scaler.</strong> You understand social scales on creative, and you can keep a diversified asset pipeline moving with the creative team. You've taken a paid social channel from small to large and kept it efficient on the way up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Efficiency-minded.</strong> You think in CAC and payback, and you can tell efficient growth from spend that just looks like growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on by choice.</strong> You'd rather be in the account driving impact than in a deck. You like the detail, and you build things yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Already building with AI.</strong> You use AI day to day, you're comfortable building agents, and you'll use Lovable to ship the tools this role runs on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical spiking</strong>. You go deep in at least one of: data analytics, data engineering, or tracking and measurement. You don't need all three at that level, but you need to be strong in one, comfortable in the rest, and delivering the work yourself.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run paid search and display end to end.</strong> Own the channels across Google, Microsoft, The Trade Desk and emerging AI surfaces like ChatGPT Ads. You set the account structure, the bids, the budgets, and the targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automate the day-to-day.</strong> Build agents and automations with Lovable that read performance, pace and shift budgets, flag issues before they cost us, and make the changes. The goal is a paid program that mostly runs itself, with you steering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale through creative.</strong> Keep a steady supply of diversified assets in market, and know which creative to push when. You've scaled Youtube before, so you know volume and variety are what keep it working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go programmatic where it pays.</strong> Use a DSP (DV360, Criteo, or The Trade Desk) to extend into prospecting, retargeting, and new inventory, and hold the same efficiency bar there as everywhere else.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Protect the signal.</strong> This is where your technical depth shows up, and you deliver it yourself rather than handing it to a data team. Build and debug the tracking (server-side/CAPI, pixels, cookies, consent, and deduplication), and write the queries that judge channels on incrementality instead of platform-reported ROAS alone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay in the details.</strong> You'll be in the accounts, running tests on audiences, bids, and creative, and building most of this yourself. This is a role for someone who wants their hands on the work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About your application</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please submit your application in English. It’s our company language, so you’ll be speaking lots of it if you join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We treat all candidates equally - if you’re interested, please apply through our careers portal.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lovable/performance-marketer-paid-search-london-361219","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794498029},{"slug":"mid-market-account-executive-london-german-speaking-449989","company_name":"Lovable","title":"Mid-Market Account Executive, London (German Speaking)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TL;DR - </strong>We’re looking for a Mid-Market Account Executive to drive Lovable’s next chapter of growth by bringing our AI-powered software creation platform to startups and enterprises across the world. You’ll own the full sales cycle - from outreach to close - turning curiosity into conviction and conviction into contracts. If you thrive on momentum, storytelling, and multi-threaded deals, this is your arena.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Lovable?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is the software creation platform that gives people the power to act on the problems closest to them. For decades, turning an idea into software required so much capital, technical fluency, and time that many ideas never came to life. Lovable is the counterargument: a platform for all people with ideas, ambition, and problems worth solving. From solopreneurs to small business owners to teams at companies like Adidas and Zendesk, people have built over 60 million projects on Lovable since its launch in November 2024. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building a generational company from Stockholm, with growing teams in London, Boston, New York, and San Francisco. Our team is small, talent-dense, and moving quickly, with a culture rooted in extreme ownership, high velocity, and low-ego collaboration. We look for people who care deeply, ship fast, and are eager to make a dent in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is one of TIME’s 100 Most Influential Companies and has been recognized on the Forbes AI 50 and CNBC Disruptor 50, reflecting our momentum as one of Europe’s fastest-growing AI companies and one of the most ambitious places to build in this next era of software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven success closing mid-market SaaS deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of closing experience, with a track record in the $50K-250K ACV range</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of full-cycle selling - prospecting, discovery, demos, negotiation, and close - working a defined target-account list</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communicator who can translate technical and product concepts into clear business value</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort running a high-velocity pipeline: deal cycles typically 30-90 days against a $600K-1.2M quota</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Builder mindset - you're excited to shape GTM motion and systems in a fast-scaling org</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity and hunger to master Lovable's product deeply; you lead with insight</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with ambiguous, high-growth environments where speed and precision matter</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling AI or developer tools, or working in product-led growth motions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Native German speaking abilities</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and run end-to-end sales cycles with precision - from first touch to signed contract, working a defined target-account list</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Craft strategic account plans that identify whitespace, map stakeholders, and unlock expansion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead compelling demos and discovery sessions, tailoring value to technical and business buyers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate cross-functionally with Product, Marketing, and Customer Success to deliver seamless onboarding and retention</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build ROI-driven business cases that connect Lovable's capabilities to real outcomes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain pipeline accuracy and forecasting discipline across all active deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use insights from customer conversations to influence product roadmap and GTM strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion a repeatable, data-driven GTM motion as we scale from startups to enterprise</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About your application</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please submit your application in English. It’s our company language so you’ll be speaking lots of it if you join.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We treat all candidates equally - if you’re interested please apply through our careers portal.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lovable/mid-market-account-executive-london-german-speaking-449989","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794498029},{"slug":"staff-analyst-risk-and-fraud-systems-uk-8752","company_name":"Paddle","title":"Staff Analyst - Risk and Fraud Systems","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What do we do?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paddle offers digital product companies a completely different approach to their payment infrastructure. Instead of assembling and maintaining a complex stack of payments-related apps and services, we’re a Merchant of Record for our customers. That means we take away 100% of the pain of payment fragmentation. It’s faster, safer, cheaper, and, above all, way better. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re backed by investors including KKR, FTV Capital, Kindred, Notion, and 83North and serve over 10,000 software sellers in 245 territories globally. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role:  </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the data, decisioning and automated systems that allow Paddle to take more good risk while reducing fraud losses, unnecessary customer friction and manual work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paddle’s Merchant of Record model makes risk a critical part of the product and its economics. Seller quality, buyer fraud, payment acceptance, refunds, disputes, reserves and card-scheme exposure cannot be optimised independently. This role will connect those signals, identify where the largest value is being lost, turn risk priorities into working controls and workflows, prove their effect in production, and establish a durable owner once a capability becomes repeatable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a strategy-only role and it is not ownership of a large operational team. It is a hands-on build role at the intersection of risk, data, product, engineering and operations.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work hands-on with SQL (Snowflake, dbt), Python, statistics and modern AI-assisted tools to explore data, test hypotheses, prototype controls and evaluate results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Map the end-to-end seller risk system, its data, decisions, controls, owners and failure points.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish the baseline before building: fraud losses, alert yield, time-to-detect, exposure at detection and analyst effort, with losses reconciled with Finance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the health of live controls: every rule and check has an owner, an expected volume, a measured yield and alerting when it goes quiet or drifts, and every change is tested and impact-assessed before release.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a labelled library of confirmed fraud cases and a shared fraud typology: the basis for rules now and for machine-learning models with Data Science later.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a value-ranked portfolio of risk opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate risk problems into clear product, data and engineering work with measurable acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design seller risk tiers that set payout timing, reserves and limits, giving good sellers more room and tightening controls on riskier ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backtest rules and risk scores on point-in-time data, and design control experiments, shadow tests and phased roll-outs that measure both loss reduction and legitimate-customer impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce decision artefacts that let senior leaders make trade-offs about risk appetite, engineering investment, customer experience and commercial growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay with each major capability until it works in production, then establish its long-term owner and move to the next high-value problem.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expected 6 month outcomes:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one major seller-risk journey has materially improved on agreed loss, approval, speed or manual-effort measures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fraud/Risk Operations spends significantly less time on repetitive screening and more time on investigation, judgement and improvement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stable capabilities have been handed to durable owners, leaving the role free to take on the next high-value problems.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We'd love to hear from you if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant experience building or improving merchant- or seller-side fraud detection at a PSP, acquirer, payfac, marketplace or Merchant of Record, and a working knowledge of how bust-out, transaction laundering and self-dealing show up in the data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on analytical ability,  fluency in SQL (Snowflake, dbt or similar), Python and statistics, plus experience using LLMs on unstructured data such as website content or support tickets, with measured accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with decision flow systems such as Tactile</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of turning ambiguous cross-functional problems into systems that were adopted and produced measurable results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing, backtesting and tuning rules and risk scores on point-in-time data, and evaluating them when labels are delayed, partial and adversarial.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A habit of treating controls as production systems: version control, testing and impact analysis on every change, monitoring that flags when a rule goes quiet or drifts, and an audit trail with human escalation for high-impact actions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to put risk trade-offs in money (fraud losses, approval rates, customer friction, operating cost and revenue from seller categories declined today) using a method Finance will sign off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good judgement about when a problem needs a rule, a workflow, an experiment, a vendor, a model or an agent—and when it needs none of them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work credibly with investigators, operators, product managers, engineers, data scientists and executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable challenging inherited assumptions while keeping the people closest to the work involved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">More interested in solving and shipping than in building an empire.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a Merchant of Record, payments, marketplace, subscription or other adversarial transactional environment is useful but not mandatory.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Everyone is welcome at Paddle</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Paddle, we’re committed to removing invisible barriers, both for our customers and within our own teams. We recognise and celebrate that every Paddler is unique and we welcome every individual perspective. As an inclusive employer, we don’t care if, or where, you studied, what you look like or where you’re from. We’re more interested in your craft, curiosity, passion for learning and what you’ll add to our culture. We encourage you to apply even if you don’t match every part of the job ad, especially if you’re part of an underrepresented group.<br /><br /><strong>Please let us know if there’s anything we can do to better support you through the application process and in the workplace. We will do everything we can to support