liver practical people support.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a hands-on partner to managers at all levels, you will use independent judgment to coach managers, resolve people issues and follow through on day-to-day work as teams scale. You will own delivery across your portfolio, working closely with the International HRBP Leader, Recruiting, Finance, Employment Legal and People centres of expertise, and involving specialist partners when needed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an individual contributor role reporting to the International HRBP Leader.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own day-to-day HRBP support with a primary focus on GTM. </strong>Be a practical point of contact for managers on performance, employee relations, team changes and development. Prioritise issues, agree clear next steps and see them through to resolution as teams scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support teams as they grow. </strong>Help managers put agreed team structures and workforce plans into practice, clarify roles and address capacity needs as teams enter new markets and scale existing operations. Coordinate with Finance and Recruiting to support hiring and team changes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build manager effectiveness. </strong>Coach managers at all levels, from first-time managers to experienced people managers, on feedback, difficult conversations, team dynamics and accountability. Help them address everyday people challenges with clarity and care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build capability and succession. </strong>Help managers identify skills and development needs across GTM teams. Partner on talent reviews, succession planning, internal mobility and development, with particular attention to roles essential to customer and business outcomes.</p></li><li