><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re proud to be supported by world-leading investors, including Energize Capital and Accel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Read more about what we’re building <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.axle.energy/blog/analysis/power-of-the-home"><strong><u>here</u></strong></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">France is one of the most important flexibility markets in Europe. This role is critical to accelerating Axle’s growth in France.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Axle has quickly become the leader in our operational markets, and we’re now looking to expand our reach in France.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the core of our market expansion plans is market analysis. To maximise future revenue, we spend a lot of time understanding the value of flexibility in power markets around the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a technical individual (data scientist, analyst or engineer) with strong knowledge of the French electricity markets and an instinct for commercial value.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will become Axle’s internal expert on French power markets: understanding the market rules, modelling the value, and building relationships with system operators and regulators. We’re scrappy about method and rigorous about conclusions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will speak fluent French and English. Other European languages will also be an asset.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will be doing</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Developing a deep understanding of French energy markets and grid dynamics to understand how trading, compensation, penalties and cash flow work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Jumping on the phone with grid operators, regulators and market stakeholders to validate hypotheses and make sense of data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building and optimising models of wholesale/NEBCO, capacity, balancing, ancillary services and local flexibility markets in France to forecast what different assets can earn</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sizing the revenue opportunity across markets and products to shape where we expand next</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building and evaluating different strategies for cycling a battery or load-shifting an EV charger</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitoring and shaping energy regulation to accelerate the growth of flexibility.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to gain unique domain expertise and build the quantitative case for first-of-a-kind projects across the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we think you need to be successful</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep quantitative and modelling ability (Python, SQL)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional communication and the ability to turn data into actionable commercial insights</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort moving fast and making decisions in an evolving environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of French electricity markets (NEBCO, Mécanisme de Capacité, Mécanisme d’Ajustement, ancillary services…)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relationships with regulators, grid operators and other stakeholders (CRE, DGEC, RTE, Enedis, etc.) are a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What’s in it for you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a 12 month fixed-term contract (CDD). Compensation is highly competitive and dependent on experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate with a deliberately flat structure and aim to keep pay equitable across the company, with a 1:1 median ratio between founder and team compensation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bi-annual retreats to strengthen team connection &amp; shared purpose.</p><p style="m