&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is looking for a Marketing &amp;amp; CRM intern to join the Experiences team in Paris for a 6-month internship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with the person in charge of Demand for Paris Experiences, alongside Marketing, Growth and Product Management partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experiences let guests step into the real life of a destination: cook with a local chef, explore a hidden neighborhood with a historian, discover Paris through the eyes of the people who live there. Paris is one of our most iconic and competitive markets, and our job on the Demand side is to make sure the right guests find the right Experience at the right moment, whether they are visiting Paris or live nearby.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a curious, organized and data-friendly student who loves the craft of CRM and Operational Marketing: a sharp brief, a well-built email, a smart audience, and an analysis that tells us what to do next. You are comfortable juggling several campaigns at once, working with different teams, and turning numbers into clear recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The difference you will make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will support the Paris Experiences Demand lead on the day-to-day CRM and marketing activity that drives bookings. You will see a campaign from the first brief to the final analysis, and you will own your own projects along the way. During your internship, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Run email campaigns end to end&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write briefs for email campaigns (audience, objective, key messages, timing) and coordinate with copy, design and CRM partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute campaigns through our internal tools and planning process, including setup, QA and send follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze results after each send (opens, clicks, bookings, incrementality) and share clear learnings and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Support listing promotion and audience targeting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze cohorts of guests (new vs. returning, local vs. traveler, International vs Domestic) to understand behavior over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build simple, readable dashboards and recurring reports to select and prioritize listings based on quality, availability, performance and fit with the campaign&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Market and Supply teams to make sure what we promote is bookable and best-in-class&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn insights into concrete recommendations for audiences, timing and messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Follow local activations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational support and follow-up on field campaigns such as flyering, partnerships, events or more: briefing, logistics, timing, partners and results tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help measure what works locally and recommend future iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The intern experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern, you will be part of a team where you contribute to real projects with real business impact. Your manager, your team and our wider employee community will strive to be superhosts to you during your internship. We provide the support, mentorship and hands-on experience you need to learn quickly and make an impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get a front-row seat on how a global marketplace builds demand for a destination, with real ownership from day one: your campaigns go live and your analyses shape decisions. You’ll do it alongside a team that cares about craft, curiosity and human connection. You can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Marketing, Market Management and Acquisition partners to deliver projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present your analyses and recommendations to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek and give feedback throughout the internship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in the Experiences and broader Airbnb community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current student or recent graduate&lt;/strong&gt; (degree completed within the last 12 months) from a leading business school, engineering school or equivalent program in France, looking for a 6-month internship starting in January 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in French and English&lt;/strong&gt;, with excellent written communication: you can write a clear brief and a clear recap. You also have an eye for great copy and for what makes a message feel human&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong interest in marketing, CRM or growth&lt;/strong&gt;, and in travel, hospitality or community-driven products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious about data and performance metrics&lt;/strong&gt;, with an interest in using insights and quantitative analysis to evaluate campaigns, track performance, and inform decision-making. Experience with Claude or other AI tools to work faster and smarter is a must-have.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented&lt;/strong&gt;, able to manage several campaigns and deadlines in parallel, and to follow up until everything is done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A collaborative mindset &lt;/strong&gt;and the confidence to work with people across teams, from Marketing to Product to Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have work authorization for France. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of this position, the successful applicant will need to be based in Paris, France to be able to conduct their work. Interns can expect to spend half of their time at the office and half working remotely with exact dates as agreed upon by the hiring manager. Additional in-person attendance for team meetings or offsites may be required as needed. Please note we are unable to provide relocation or visa sponsorship for this position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our commitment to inclusion &amp;amp; belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future.&amp;nbsp; This role may also be eligible for benefits and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;France Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€25.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€25.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/airbnb/marketing-crm-intern-experiences-paris-396246","tags":["Intern"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794412533},{"slug":"senior-talent-partner-tech-paris-5757","company_name":"Dust","title":"Senior Talent Partner, Tech","description":"<h1><strong>About Dust</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work is being rewritten, and the people holding the pen are the ones who actually run it.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With enterprise-grade governance, flexible model choice, and a collaborative interface for humans and agents to work together, Dust empowers AI Operators at the world’s fastest-moving companies to rewire how work gets done.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 70%+ weekly active users, people stick with Dust as much as they do with Slack and Notion. We don't get piloted and shelved. We land once, and spread. <strong>We're at an exciting stage of our journey, and growing fast.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're serving <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://dust.tt/customers">great customers</a> like Datadog, 1Password, Cursor, Clay, Vanta and Persona, and aim to x5 our growth by the end of 2026.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dust is backed by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://techcrunch.com/2024/06/27/dust-grabs-another-16-million-for-its-enterprise-ai-assistants-connected-to-internal-data/">Sequoia</a> with a determined team of optimists (coming from Stripe, OpenAI, and Stanford) who like to focus on users, ship fast, and don't take themselves too seriously while doing so. The Generalist <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/dust-tt_were-honored-to-be-recognized-on-the-generalists-activity-7359284343929741313-Rq04">named us among the Future 50</a>.</p><h1><strong>Why this role exists</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are about to hire the people who will define the next phase of this company. Not backfill a plan someone else wrote — define it. The quality of who joins Dust over the next eighteen months is the single highest-leverage variable in whether we build the category or watch someone else do it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">That work needs a recruiter who treats hiring as a craft rather than a queue. Someone who can hold a real point of view on what "great" looks like for a role, defend it with a hiring manager who disagrees, and then go find that person themselves — from a cold start, without a lead gen team, a sourcing pod, or a playbook waiting for them.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be an early member of a small Talent team. That means you own roles end to end, and you also help build the thing itself: the assessment design, the interview loops, the calibration, the data we use to know whether any of it is working.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who cares about the candidate experience for all parties internal and external. And prioritizes protecting Dust's culture by being thoughtful, thorough and leading by example in being a true team player.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What you'll own</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Full-cycle hiring, end to end.</strong> You run your own searches from role kickoff to close. Sourcing, outreach, screening, interviewing, offer strategy, negotiation. You are the owner of the outcome, not a coordinator of other people's opinions.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Assessment design, not just assessment delivery.</strong> For every role you open, you help define what evidence would actually predict success — then you build the loop that surfaces it. You'll push back on interview stages that exist out of habit and replace them with ones that test something real.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring manager partnership with a spine.</strong> You'll spend as much time calibrating hiring managers as you do talking to candidates. When a manager says "not quite the right feel," you'll ask what they mean until there's a defensible answer, and you'll say so when there isn't one.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market intelligence.</strong> You'll know your talent market better than anyone else in the building — who's good, where they are, what moves them, what compensation actually looks like right now — and you'll bring that back into how we scope roles and design offers.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The candidate experience.</strong> Our hiring process is the first honest sample of what working here feels like. You'll make it expedient, direct, well-communicated, and worth a candidate's time whether or not they get an offer.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Building the function.</strong> Process, tooling, structured scorecards, funnel data, quality-of-hire signal. You'll leave the system better than you found it, and you'll be trusted to change it without asking permission first.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Two tracks — tell us which one is yours</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring for depth in one of two areas. You should have a genuine centre of gravity in one; interest in the other is a bonus, not a requirement.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>GTM.</strong> Account Executives, Sales Engineers, Customer Success, Marketing, and the leaders above them, across Europe and the US. You know how to assess commercial talent on evidence rather than swagger, and you can tell the difference between a rep who carried a territory and a rep who inherited one.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical.</strong> Software engineers, infrastructure, product, and design, in a market where the best people are not looking and the second-best are drowning in outreach. You can hold a credible conversation about what someone actually built, and you know why that matters more than where they built it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>How we think about hiring</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're telling you this up front because if you disagree with it, this will be a frustrating job.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We don't hire based on pedigree.</strong> Logos and school names are weak evidence. What someone has actually done, and what they can demonstrate now, is strong evidence. We design our loops accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We hire for evidence, not affinity.</strong> "Culture fit" that means "reminds me of me" is how companies get homogeneous and slow. We assess against explicit behaviours tied to how we work, and we write down what we saw.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speed and rigour are not in tension.</strong> Slow processes are usually a symptom of unclear thinking about the role, not of high standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A no should be as clear as a yes.</strong> To the candidate, and internally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Some of us came from well-known companies.</strong> That's context, not criteria. It isn't why we're here and it won't be why you are. We celebrate everyone's achievements and want to create an environment where diversity of thought and experience of a collective whole makes this place exceptional and lasting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Recruiters are operators, not order-takers.</strong> If you think a role is wrongly scoped, badly levelled, or shouldn't be open at all, you're expected to say so.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in full-cycle recruiting, with meaningful time in-house at a high-growth company. You've hired in an environment with real ambiguity, not just real volume.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrable depth in either GTM or technical hiring — you can talk through searches you've run, what made them hard, and what you'd do differently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuinely strong sourcing. Not "I partner with a sourcing team." You find people yourself, and you write outreach that people reply to because it's obviously written by a human who read something.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating without infrastructure. No playbook, no SDR equivalent, limited tooling to start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The judgement and directness to challenge senior stakeholders, and the credibility to be listened to when you do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bias to start. You see the gap and close it before anyone asks you to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written English and a real feel for language. Everything you write is a piece of our employer brand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Low ego, high ownership. No job is too big or too small — you'll design an assessment framework in the morning and chase a scheduling conflict in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Paris, London or New York.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ideal, but not required:</strong> experience hiring in AI or developer-facing companies; experience building or improving a hiring process rather than inheriting one; multi-market hiring across Europe and the US.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>You'll be using AI to do this job — properly</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build the AI operating system that companies use to rewire their work. We expect our own team to be the sharpest possible example of that.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll build and run your own Dust agents: market maps, candidate research, interview debrief synthesis, competitive intelligence on where talent is moving. Not as a side project — as how the job gets done. You don't need to have done this before, but you do need to be the kind of person who is genuinely excited to, rather than politely tolerant of it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also be one of our most credible internal sources of feedback on the product, because you'll be a heavy user of it every day.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in Paris, London or New York, and we'd love you to spend real time in the office with the team. A lot of the best things about building at Dust happen because people are in the same room: the energy, the fast decisions, the unexpected conversation that unlocks a hard problem.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire people with strong judgement and extend that trust to how they manage their time.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Our process</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'll tell you the full loop up front, keep it to a small number of stages, and give you a decision quickly. You'll meet the people you'd work with, not a panel of proxies. Expect at least one stage where you work through a real hiring problem with us rather than describing a past one.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don't check every box, apply anyway. We're more interested in your potential and how you think than a perfect match to a checklist.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please send your application and resume in English.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're prioritizing building our team with an in-person culture at our offices in Paris, London, San Francisco, and New York because we value the magic that happens when talented people work closely together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have an office-first culture. Some of the best things about building at Dust are the energy, the fast decisions, and the unexpected conversations that unlock a hard problem, which happen because we are in the same room. Being together is not a formality, it is how we do our best work, and it is something we actively protect.<br /><br />That said, we hire people with strong judgement and we extend that trust to how they manage their time. When working from home makes more sense for what you need to get done that day, we trust you to make that call.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Why Dust</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The models are powerful enough. What's missing is the product layer where AI meets how companies actually work. That's what we're building: the infrastructure that lets any team turn scattered knowledge and tools into coordinated execution with agents they build, own, and run themselves.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use Dust ourselves every day. We get to shape how humans and agents collaborate while solving our own problems with the product we ship. That loop is rare, and it's why we move fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about defining a new category and want to join a determined team of optimists who focus on users, ship fast, and don't take themselves too seriously, we'd love to talk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Even if you don't check every box in our requirements, we encourage you to apply. We value diverse perspectives and backgrounds, and we're more interested in your potential and passion than a perfect match to our checklist. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learn how we think and work.</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blog.dust.tt/a-first-version-of-our-product-constitution/">Our product constitution,</a> <em>a story about our mission</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all font-semibold transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out hover:underline text-highlight hover:text-highlight-400 active:text-highlight-dark" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xIvlRWEXqqw">Your Next Co-Worker Isn’t Human</a>, <strong>Stanislas Polu</strong>, VivaTech 2026. A conversation about AI agents taking on larger parts of work and how teams collaborate with them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all font-semibold transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out hover:underline text-highlight hover:text-highlight-400 active:text-highlight-dark" href="https://www.nasdaq.com/videos/dust">Dust: Gabriel Hubert on Enterprise AI</a>, <strong>Gabriel Hubert</strong>, Nasdaq, published May 7, 2026. On Dust’s approach to enterprise AI and building the company in Europe.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/dust/senior-talent-partner-tech-paris-5757","tags":["Talent"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794411620},{"slug":"enterprise-platform-architect-76081-bern-355575","company_name":"IQ Plus AG","title":"(Enterprise) Platform Architect (76081)","description":"<p>Wir suchen für einen unserer Kunden (Enterprise) Platform Architekten für ein ganzes Managed Capacity Team. Das Ziel ist es eine übergreifende Architektur (weiter-)zu entwickeln. Dabei ist zu klären, welche Themen / Fähigkeiten übergreifend, welche spezifisch für gewisse AI-Einsatzgebiete sind und welche lokal (je Projekt / Anwendung) gelöst werden.</p>
<p>Starke Faktoren für die Gestaltung der Architektur sind  </p>
<p>• Sicherheit (Bedrohungen von aussen, von innen): Identität und Berechtigungen, Datenschutz und Datenklassifizierung.  </p>
<p>• Regulatorik und Compliance, Nachvollziehbarkeit und Audit  </p>
<p>• Enabling (AI Technologien einfach nutzbar machen, Self-Service, automatisierte Compliance)  </p>
<p>• Kosten und Wirtschaftlichkeit  </p>
<p>• Qualität und Verlässlichkeit, Betrieb und Resilienz  </p>
<p>• Passung in die bestehende IT-Landschaft, Migrationsfähigkeit  </p>
<p>• Integration und Interoperabilität</p>
<p>Das Team arbeitet eng mit den verantwortlichen Stellen und Fachpersonen des Endkunden zusammen.  </p>
<p>Gesucht werden Personen mit ausgewiesener Erfahrung in der Konzeption und Weiterentwicklung komplexer Enterprise- und Plattformarchitekturen. Erwartet wird insbesondere die Fähigkeit, strategische Zielbilder in konkrete Architekturentscheidungen, Standards, Plattformfähigkeiten und umsetzbare Roadmaps zu überführen.</p>
<ul>
<li>Ausgewiesene Erfahrung mit AI-/GenAI-Architekturen in grossen Organisationen.</li>
<li>Fundiertes Verständnis von LLMs, RAG, agentischen Systemen und Protokollen wie MCP oder A2A sowie ihren Risiken (Prompt Injection, Datenabfluss, Halluzinationen)</li>
<li>Erfahrung mit Security-by-Design: Identity & Access Management (auch für nicht-menschliche Identitäten und Agenten), Datenklassifizierung, Zero Trust</li>
<li>Fähigkeit, komplexe Architektur für unterschiedliche Zielgruppen verständlich darzustellen, vom Management bis zum Entwicklungsteam</li>
<li>Deutsch verhandlungssicher, Englisch gut</li>
<li>Mindestens 2 Referenzen in der Konzeption oder Umsetzung von AI-Plattformen oder Shared Services, z.B. AI Gateway, Model Hub, Agent Runtime, Vector Stores, Knowledge Management</li>
