obs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/twojobs/projektmanager-fe-sursee-420304","tags":["Project Management"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","teamleitung"],"location":"Sursee","created_at":1794477747},{"slug":"principal-design-engineer-mechanical-equipment-80-100-zurich-483998","company_name":"Climeworks","title":"Principal Design Engineer - Mechanical Equipment (80-100%)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Lead technically by doing.</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">Join our Design Engineering team as a highly experienced individual contributor. You will take on challenging mechanical design problems yourself, from concepts and CAD models to manufacturing drawings, prototypes and tested hardware, while helping the wider team make strong technical decisions.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">As a Principal Design Engineer, you are a hands-on member of our Design Engineering team, designing Climeworks’ CO2 collectors, the heart of our direct air capture plant. Improving how they perform, are manufactured and scale is central to the future success of DAC.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Mechanical concept &amp; product design:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You personally turn new concepts into robust physical products: developing mechanical concepts, creating CAD models, designing components and complete collector assemblies, producing manufacturing drawings, and supporting hardware through fabrication, assembly and testing.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Engineering problem-solving &amp; risk reduction:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Your experience helps you find the right solutions faster, anticipate problems early and reduce risk before issues reach manufacturing or testing.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">CO2 collector design:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You take mechanical systems from requirements and concepts through to detailed, manufacturable designs. You develop solutions, perform engineering calculations and make the decisions needed to create robust industrial hardware.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">First-principles engineering:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You use experience and first-principles reasoning to identify risks early, evaluate alternatives quickly and converge on simple, robust solutions. You apply calculations, tolerance analysis, design reviews and testing to reduce uncertainty.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Own design from concept to commercialisation:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You work directly in SolidWorks to create and modify parts, assemblies and system layouts. You manage complex interfaces, packaging constraints and design changes so the complete system works together. You produce and maintain high-quality 2D manufacturing drawings, including appropriate GD&amp;T, tolerances, materials, finishes and manufacturing requirements.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Prototype fabrication, assembly &amp; testing:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You stay closely involved after the CAD work is complete. You support prototype fabrication, assembly and testing, investigate issues and incorporate the learning back into the design.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Technical leadership &amp; design reviews:</span></strong><span style="colo