&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The pay range for this role is based on relative market data and alignment with our compensation philosophy. The range displayed reflects the minimum and maximum of the pay range for each job posting, which is used to determine new hire rates/salaries and takes into consideration multiple factors including but not limited to knowledge, skills, abilities, proficiencies, experience, education, &lt;span class=&quot;WGI1&quot;&gt;licensures/certifications,&lt;/span&gt; as well as business and organizational needs. nCino reserves the right to modify the posted range consistent with our internal practices and external market movement. The recruiter for this job posting can share more compensation details during the recruitment process, as base salary is only one component of the total compensation package per position posted.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The base salary range for this job is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£63,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£107,400 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;nCino provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran status, disability, genetics or other protected groups. In addition to federal law requirements, nCino complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the company has facilities. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation and training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;nCino is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, nCino will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations. If reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other benefits and privileges of employment, please contact us at &lt;a ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to inclusion and equality includes a strong belief that the diversity of our team is instrumental to our success.&amp;nbsp; We strive to create workplaces where employees are empowered to bring their authentic selves to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _2rkolb4i _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;https://www.ncino.com/ncino-applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-is-router-link=&quot;false&quot; data-testid=&quot;link-with-safety&quot;&gt;Please view our Applicant Privacy Policy here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/ncinoinc/principal-project-manager-148710","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1794380115},{"slug":"deployed-engineering-manager-northern-europe-dach-amsterdam-6336","company_name":"LangChain","title":"Deployed Engineering Manager, Northern Europe & DACH","description":"<h1><strong>About Us</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At LangChain, our mission is to make intelligent agents ubiquitous. We build the foundation for agent engineering in the real world, helping developers move from prototypes to production-ready AI agents that teams can rely on. We began as widely adopted open-source tools and have grown to also offer a platform for building, evaluating, deploying, and operating agents at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With $125M raised at Series B from IVP, Sequoia, Benchmark, CapitalG, and Sapphire Ventures, we’re at a stage where we’re continuing to develop new products, growth is accelerating, and all team members have meaningful impact on what we build and how we work together. LangChain is a place where your contributions can shape how this technology shows up in the real world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, our platform includes LangSmith (Observability, Evaluation, Deployment, Fleet, and Sandboxes), our open source frameworks (LangChain, LangGraph, and Deep Agents), and the newly launched LangSmith Engine for autonomous agent improvement. We have 100M+ monthly open source downloads, 6,000+ active LangSmith customers, and 5 of the Fortune 10 use LangSmith in production (+ 35% of the Fortune 500 overall), including teams at Klarna, Clay, Coinbase, Workday, Lyft, Cloudflare, Harvey, Rippling, Vanta, LinkedIn, Monday.com, Nvidia, and Bridgewater.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Deployed Engineering Manager for Northern Europe, you will lead a team of deployed engineers from our hub in Amsterdam, working with our customers across DACH and Benelux. You'll help build and shape the team, grow the people in it and make sure our customers get the technical partnership they need to build and run great agents in production. This is an opportunity to have outsized impact at a company shaping the future of AI-powered software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">DEs work alongside our sales team to help our prospects and customers build reliable, scalable agents for their business using our suite of products: LangChain, LangGraph, Deep Agents and LangSmith. The team focuses on pre-sales efforts, but stays on accounts to not only close new business but also to make our customers wildly successful.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your first job is your people. You will support great deployed engineers, ramp them quickly, coach them through live customer work and build a team where they do the best work of their careers. You'll stay close enough to the technology and to our customers to be credible with both: unblocking your team on hard engagements and stepping in on the region's most important opportunities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will report to the Director of Deployed Engineering, EMEA and partner closely with LangChain's sales leaders covering DACH and Benelux, with shared ownership of regional outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is mostly people leadership, with real customer engagement and revenue accountability alongside it. As part of the EMEA deployed engineering leadership team, you'll also bring what you learn back into the playbooks, processes and standards we use globally.<br /></p><h2>What You'll Do:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow the DACH/Benelux DE team</strong>: support recruiting, interviewing and closing candidates as the team grows and raise the bar with every hire.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Onboard and ramp new DEs quickly</strong>, with a clear definition of what "ramped" looks like and the support to get each person there.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coach your team through live customer work</strong>: join calls, review architectures and proofs of value to provide direct, specific feedback that makes people better.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own performance management</strong>: set clear expectations, recognise great work and address underperformance early and fairly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run the team's operating rhythm</strong>: account coverage, capacity and load balancing, deal and engagement reviews and the regional cadence with sales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner with sales leadership in DACH and the Benelux</strong> on account strategy, coverage and technical win plans, with shared accountability for revenue outcomes and customer success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring regional insight to the global DE team</strong>: what's working with customers in the region, product feedback and contributions to shared playbooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Develop future leaders</strong>, growing the senior DEs who will lead the next teams in the region.</p></li></ul><h2><br />How to be successful in the role:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of experience in sales engineering, solutions architecture, engineering, or similar customer-facing technical roles at a dev tools, AI, or infrastructure company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years managing customer-facing engineers, including hiring, coaching and performance management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of developing people: engineers you hired and grew who went on to bigger scope or roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical credibility with your team and your customers: you're not a stranger to Python, and are well-versed in software engineering, platform engineering and solutions architecture. Hands-on experience building with LLMs or agents is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with or selling to developers and engineering-led buyers and an understanding of how enterprises in the region evaluate and buy (procurement, data protection, hosting and sovereignty requirements).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional communication and technical storytelling skills, with the ability to simplify complex concepts for customers and coach others to do the same.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bias for action, comfort with ambiguity and a consistently high bar for excellence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English; German strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Must be available to work in Amsterdam, with regular travel across the region.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation Philosophy:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer competitive compensation that includes base salary, variable compensation for relevant roles, meaningful equity, benefits, and perks. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hiring for this role across a range of scope, and the compensation band reflects that. Your offer depends on what we learn about your impact, craft, leadership, and communication during the interview process. We will tell you early where you’re tracking and talk comp with you before offer stage. Team members in the EU, UK, and APAC receive locally competitive benefits aligned with regional norms and regulations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Benefits</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benefits include medical, dental, and vision coverage, flexible vacation, a 401(k) plan, meals on in-office days in the US and more.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/langchain/deployed-engineering-manager-northern-europe-dach-amsterdam-6336","tags":["Deployed Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794379212},{"slug":"senior-corporate-recruiter-amsterdam-351670","company_name":"Testendouble","title":"Senior Corporate Recruiter","description":"&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role in Our Story:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;As a Senior Recruiter at ACT, you will attract and hire commercial talent, primarily -and not alone- for our Front Office teams. You will manage the recruitment process from intake to offer, working closely with hiring managers to understand their business, challenge requirements and turn hiring needs into effective recruitment strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You understand our markets and what motivates people working in environmental commodities, energy and trading. You use this knowledge to identify talent, build relationships and give practical advice on how to attract the right candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 []&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the full recruitment cycle, primarily for Front Office positions, including sales, trading and business development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with hiring managers to define role requirements, agree on selection criteria and keep recruitment moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proactively source and engage candidates, building talent pipelines for current and future hiring needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bring market knowledge into hiring discussions, advising on talent availability, competitor activity and candidate expectations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conduct thorough interviews and support objective, consistent hiring decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliver a positive candidate experience through clear communication, timely feedback and careful follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keep Greenhouse accurate and up to date, using recruitment data to identify bottlenecks and improve results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work closely with fellow recruiters, HR and Employer Branding, sharing knowledge and contributing to team priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates with the following qualifications and attributes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3–5 years of recruitment experience, with a strong track record of hiring for commercial or Front Office positions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of environmental commodities, energy, trading or closely related financial and commodity markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong sourcing skills and experience engaging passive candidates in competitive international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Confidence working with hiring managers, offering practical advice and respectfully challenging assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An eager, proactive approach: you take initiative, spot opportunities and follow through.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A collaborative mindset: you share insights, support colleagues and take responsibility for team results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage several vacancies and changing priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience using an ATS, preferably Greenhouse, and an interest in applying recruitment technology and AI effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent communication skills in English and the ability to connect with people across different cultures and backgrounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet these criteria and are ready to contribute your expertise to a dynamic and challenging environment, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/testendouble/senior-corporate-recruiter-amsterdam-351670","tags":["Talent Acquisition"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794369319},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-amsterdam-261496","company_name":"Auterion","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","description":"&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will play a pivotal role in the successful development, integration and deployment of Auterion-powered drone systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will collaborate closely with the production, hardware engineering, and firmware/software teams, as well as operations, ensuring that every platform transitions smoothly from an airframe concept into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. You will serve as the primary technical interface for partners, work closely with them to understand their technical requirements, configure and adapt existing solutions, contribute to core software development, and ensure successful implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys combining hands-on technical work with customer collaboration and system-level problem solving, bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage software releases and perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 or adjacent autopilot ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep avionics and airframe expertise, including autopilot tuning, sensor and payload integration, power systems and airworthiness considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to troubleshoot integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to escalate complex challenges when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical authority in customer engagements, translating mission requirements into concrete system architectures and demonstrable solutions built on AuterionOS and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance, resolving technical issues often directly in the field during customer trials and demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and continuous improvement of engineering processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and market requirements back into product and engineering teams to influence the roadmap of the Auterion stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Electrical, Mechanical, Aerospace or Robotics Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in C/C++ and Python: you can read, debug and patch existing code and write small tools and scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments, including the command line, logs, Docker and basic networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware-software integration: system bring-up, wiring and connectors, and embedded interfaces (UART, CAN, I2C, SPI) at a practical level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured troubleshooting: you can isolate whether a problem is software, hardware, configuration or RF, often under time pressure in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator: you can explain technical issues clearly to customers and operators, and report findings back to engineering in a way they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel and work on-site with customers, including at test ranges and in field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship (required for security clearance and customer requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or ArduPilot, MAVLink, QGroundControl or mission planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UAV flight testing and validation in operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with datalinks and radio systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous customer-facing or field engineering role, especially with defense or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/auterion/forward-deployed-engineer-amsterdam-261496","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794369318},{"slug":"hr-medewerker-senior-marknesse-222803","company_name":"Koninklijk Nederlands Lucht- en Ruimtevaartcentrum","title":"HR Medewerker Senior (m/v/x)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Een ervaren HR-professional die graag complexe HR-vraagstukken oppakt, kennis deelt, overzicht houdt en bijdraagt aan een goede HR-dienstverlening.</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Voor onze volop in beweging zijnde HR administratie/HR-support team zoeken we een ervaren HR-professional die goed thuis is in HR operatie en graag meedenkt over uiteenlopende HR-vraagstukken. Je bent een inhoudelijke vraagbaak voor collega’s en steekt zelf graag de handen uit de mouwen. Met een proactieve blik kijk je verder dan de dagelijkse praktijk en zie je kansen om processen te verbeteren. Herken jij jezelf hierin en bouw je graag mee aan de verdere ontwikkeling van onze afdeling? Solliciteer dan snel!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Wat ga je doen?</h4><p class="MsoNormal">Jij zorgt er samen met je hr-collega’s voor dat de basis van onze HR-administratie op orde is, maar jouw meerwaarde zit vooral in het behandelen van complexere operationele HR-vraagstukken, het ondersteunen van HR collega’s en het samen met de teamleider verder ontwikkelen van onze dienstverlening. Je bent een inhoudelijke vraagbaak voor het HR-team en een vertrouwd aanspreekpunt voor NLR medewerkers en HR-adviseurs.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Als senior HR medewerker heb je een veelzijdige rol waarin HR-administratie, dienstverlening, inhoudelijke expertise en procesverbetering samenkomen. Jouw HR collega’s houden zich bezig met de dagelijkse HR-processen, waarbij jij je richt op vooral vraagstukken die meer ervaring, inzicht en zelfstandigheid vragen. Daarnaast deel je actief je kennis met collega's, denk je mee over een slimme verdeling van het werk en draag je bij aan de kwaliteit van onze dienstverlening.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Jouw werkzaamheden in het kort:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst"><strong>Vraagbaak voor het HR-team</strong>: je behandelt tweedelijns HR-vraagstukken over bijvoorbeeld arbeidsvoorwaarden, personeelsregelingen en HR processen, detachering, inleen en deelt je kennis en ondersteunt collega’s.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle"><strong>Samenwerken met de teamleider HR</strong>: je werkt aan HR-projecten, verbetert processen en bewaakt de voortgang, met name bij piekmomenten.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle"><strong>Ondersteunen van de HR Adviseurs en managers</strong>: je helpt bij operationele HR-vraagstukken en zorgt voor een goede aansluiting tussen HR-processen en de praktijk.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle"><strong>Zorgen voor goede HR-dienstverlening</strong>: je bewaakt de kwaliteit van de HR-administratie en hebt contact met medewerkers. Je draagt bij aan een juiste en tijdige verwerking van personeelsgegevens en ondersteunt waar nodig bij eerstelijnsvragen.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast"><strong>Bouwen aan de HR-afdeling</strong>: je signaleert knelpunten, denkt mee over praktische/operationele verbeteringen, helpt werkprocessen te uniformeren en deelt je kennis met collega's.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Wat breng je mee?</h4><p class="MsoNormal">We zoeken iemand die senioriteit laat zien in zowel gedrag als HR-kennis. Je hoeft niet alles te weten, maar je hebt een stevige basis, durft verantwoordelijkheid te nemen en weet wanneer je zelfstandig kunt handelen en wanneer afstemming nodig is. First time right is het devies, kwalitatieve en zorgvuldige HR administratie en dienstverlening vinden wij belangrijk.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Verder breng je mee:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">Afgeronde opleiding in HRM of een vergelijkbare richting met minimaal vijf jaar relevante ervaring binnen HR, bij voorkeur in een brede HR-administratieve functie en kennis van AFAS.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Je hebt gedegen kennis van HR administratie en support en ervaring met het zelfstandig behandelen van HR-vraagstukken over bijvoorbeeld arbeidsvoorwaarden en personeelsregelingen.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Je bent communicatief sterk, toegankelijk en klantgericht. Je maakt gemakkelijk contact met medewerkers en collega’s op verschillende niveaus.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Je werkt graag samen, durft je eigen perspectief in te brengen en staat open voor feedback en andere inzichten.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Je werkt nauwkeurig, hebt oog voor details en houdt overzicht en helpt collega’s om werkzaamheden goed en tijdig af te ronden.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Je bent gewend en krijgt er energie van om in een snel groeiende en veranderende organisatie te werken.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Je beheerst het Nederlands en Engels goed, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk op C1 niveau.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h4>Wat bieden wij jou?</h4><p class="MsoNormal">Bij NLR krijg je de ruimte om impact te maken én jezelf te ontwikkelen. Je werkt in een innovatieve nationale en internationale hightechomgeving waar nieuwsgierigheid, samenwerking en vakmanschap centraal staan. We geloven dat mensen het beste presteren als ze de vrijheid krijgen om initiatief te nemen, zich te blijven ontwikkelen en een gezonde balans te vinden tussen werk en privé.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Verder bieden we je onder andere:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">Een bruto maandsalaris tussen € 4400,- en € 5000 <em>(op basis van een 40-urige werkweek)</em>, afhankelijk van je kennis en ervaring;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">45 verlofdagen <em>(op basis van een 40-urige werkweek);</em></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">8% vakantiegeld én een vaste eindejaarsuitkering van 8%;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">De kosten voor reizen met het openbaar vervoer worden volledig vergoed. Reis je met eigen vervoer? Dan ontvang je een kilometervergoeding voor woon-werkverkeer.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Een zorgtoelage van €145,- bruto<em> (op basis van een 40-urige werkweek) </em>via onze collectieve zorgverzekering bij OHRA als extra ondersteuning voor jouw zorgkosten;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Extra betaald ouderschapsverlof;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Volop kansen om te blijven leren met opleidingen, trainingen, coaching en andere ontwikkelmogelijkheden;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">De mogelijkheid om 32-40 uur per week te werken inclusief thuiswerken.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Jouw nieuwe werkomgeving</h4><p class="MsoNormal">Je wordt onderdeel van een breed HR-team met verschillende expertises, van HR-advies en beleid tot recruitment en Learning &amp; Development. We sparren graag met elkaar, houden elkaar scherp en inspireren elkaar om verder te komen. Er is volop ruimte voor jouw ideeën, kennis en initiatief, met oog voor elkaar en het gezamenlijke resultaat. Samen werken we aan HR-dienstverlening die aansluit bij de behoeften van de organisatie en bijdraagt aan onze strategische ambities.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Onze HR-afdeling is volop in ontwikkeling en werkt aan verdere professionalisering en verbetering van processen en samenwerking. Dat biedt kansen, maar vraagt ook iets van jou. Je komt terecht in een HR-afdeling waar we volop werken aan het verbeteren van onze dienstverlening. We brengen meer structuur aan, maken onze processen eenvoudiger en werken steeds nauwer samen. Dat betekent dat niet alles al vastligt en dat er ruimte is om mee te denken en dingen slimmer te organiseren. Je standplaats is <strong>Amsterdam</strong> of <strong>Marknesse</strong>, maar je bent ook regelmatig op onze andere locatie voor overleg en samenwerking met collega’s.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Wat betekent werken bij NLR?</h4><p class="MsoNormal">Koninklijke NLR is al meer dan 100 jaar een toonaangevende kennisinstelling voor toegepast onderzoek in de lucht- en ruimtevaart. Samen met meer dan 1000 professionals werken we aan innovatieve oplossingen voor een duurzamere, veiligere en efficiëntere lucht- en ruimtevaart. We willen dat iedereen bij NLR de ruimte krijgt om zichzelf te zijn, talenten te ontwikkelen en ideeën in te brengen. Door verschillen te waarderen en van elkaar te leren, creëren we samen een inclusieve werkomgeving.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Wil jij meer weten?</h4><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">Mail dan met Christel Bouwers (Recruiter) via <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yE9A1H8e3cg"><span style="color:#5A5F72">Onze collega’s vertellen jou graag</span></a><span style="color:#5A5F72">&nbsp;hoe het is om bij NLR te werken. Vergeet trouwens ook niet eens een kijkje op onze socials te nemen zoals ons&nbsp;</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.youtube.com/@NLRmedia"><span style="colo