 /><br />If you're this person, we'd love to talk to you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a <strong>Mobile UI Designer</strong> to create elegant, intuitive and high-performing mobile experiences for BJAK's AI Neobank and financial products.<br /><br />This role is for someone who loves designing mobile interfaces that feel effortless, responsive and visually refined. You'll work alongside engineers and product managers to create experiences used daily by millions of users.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design beautiful and intuitive interfaces for iOS and Android applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create wireframes, user flows, prototypes and production-ready UI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design mobile experiences across insurance, payments, claims, investments and financial services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain mobile design systems and reusable components.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with developers to ensure pixel-perfect implementation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optimize interfaces for usability, accessibility and platform guidelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Iterate designs using analytics, usability findings and product feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure consistency across different devices, screen sizes and operating systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years of experience designing mobile applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong portfolio showcasing high-quality mobile UI work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert proficiency in Figma and interactive prototyping.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of iOS Human Interface Guidelines and Android Material Design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of mobile usability, responsive layouts and interaction design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent attention to typography, spacing, colour and visual hierarchy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to simplify complex financial workflows into clean mobile experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Portfolio is required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Design Stack</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Figma</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">FigJam</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design Systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Auto Layout</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interactive Prototyping</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">iOS Human Interface Guidelines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Material Design</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Kind of Builder We Want</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thinks mobile-first.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obsesses over visual polish and interaction quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notices small UI inconsistencies before users do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cares about accessibility, responsiveness and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborates closely with engineers to deliver high-quality products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Takes pride in shipping pixel-perfect interfaces.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>This Role Is Not For</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designers whose experience is primarily marketing or branding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People who design without considering real user behaviour.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designers unfamiliar with mobile platform conventions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Individuals who struggle to collaborate with engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates who cannot explain the rationale behind their design decisions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is remote, but candidates must be based in <strong>Netherlands</strong>. We are hiring specifically for this market, so applicants should already be based in <strong>Netherlands</strong>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Language</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">English is our primary working language across our global teams. Strong English communication skills are required.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Interview Process</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process is designed to move fast:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Portfolio review</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical design task (if applicable)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Role-specific interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CEO / Final interview</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">For strong candidates, we aim to complete the process and make an offer within <strong>1 week</strong> from the start of the interview process. Candidates who complete assessments promptly will be prioritized.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/bjak/mobile-ui-designer-netherlands-347031","tags":["Creative/Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1794346823},{"slug":"product-designer-ui-ux-netherlands-163979","company_name":"Bjak","title":"Product Designer (UI/UX)","description":"<h1><strong>About BJAK</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">The original mission of BJAK is we believe people deserve smarter ways to plan, save and grow their money. This is the origin of our name.<br /><br />Started in 2019, we built the first mobile-first, insurance platform, enabling insurance to be accessible online by millions in the region. Today, its the leading insurance platform in Southeast Asia.<br /><br />Today, we are expanding ways to help people in the region — this includes spending, saving, investing, exchanging, travelling, and more. Our mission is help people get more from their money every day.<br /><br />We have teams working around the world, with over 20 nationalities from our offices and remotely, who truly enjoys their work. We are looking for the most talented and driven people we can find. We are looking for people who work for their passion, not counting hours. Who loves building great next-generation products, not status quo. Who cares about redefining how everyone around us can get the best financial applications, not for an exclusive few.<br /><br />If you're this person, we'd love to talk to you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a <strong>Product Designer</strong> to shape intuitive, high-quality product experiences across BJAK's financial products.<br /><br />This role is for someone who enjoys solving product problems through thoughtful interface design. You'll work closely with product managers and engineers to simplify complex financial workflows into experiences that feel fast, intuitive and trustworthy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design end-to-end product experiences from concept to production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transform product requirements into user flows, wireframes, prototypes and polished interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design intuitive experiences across insurance, payments, claims, investments and other financial products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain scalable design systems and reusable UI components.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with engineers to ensure designs are implemented accurately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve usability through rapid iteration using product data and user feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain consistency across mobile and web experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously refine interactions, accessibility and overall product quality.</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience designing digital products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong portfolio demonstrating product thinking and excellent visual design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced proficiency in Figma and interactive prototyping.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of design systems, component libraries and responsive design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of information architecture and user flows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent visual design skills including typography, spacing, layout and interaction design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to simplify complex workflows into intuitive experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Portfolio is required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Design Stack</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Figma</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">FigJam</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design Systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interactive Prototyping</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Auto Layout</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Component Libraries</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>The Kind of Builder We Want</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thinks about solving customer problems, not just designing screens.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balances business goals with user experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obsesses over clarity, simplicity and consistency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Works collaboratively with engineers and product teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Takes ownership from idea through launch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously improves products using real user insights.</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>This Role Is Not For</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designers who only focus on visuals without considering usability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People who require fully detailed specifications before contributing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designers who struggle to explain design decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Individuals who don't enjoy fast-moving startup environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates who exaggerate ownership or cannot explain what they personally designed.</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is remote, but candidates must be based in <strong>Netherlands</strong>. We are hiring specifically for this market, so applicants should already be based in <strong>Netherlands</strong>.</p><h1><br /><strong>Language</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">English is our primary working language across global teams. Strong English communication is required.</p><h1><br /><strong>Interview Process</strong></h1><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Portfolio Review</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical Design Task (if applicable)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Role-specific Interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CEO / Final Interview</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">For strong candidates, we aim to complete the process and make an offer within one week.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/bjak/product-designer-ui-ux-netherlands-163979","tags":["Creative/Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1794346823},{"slug":"senior-integration-software-engineer-amsterdam-441860","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior Integration Software Engineer","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW75090954 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;">We are looking for a hands-on <strong>Senior</strong> <strong>Integration</strong> <strong>Software Engineer</strong> to ensure the quality and reliability of software solutions used in real-world sensing and data processing systems.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW75090954 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;">Optics11 is a deep-tech company developing advanced fiber-optic sensing technologies for challenging environments and applications in energy and underwater security. Our systems enable high-performance sensing and monitoring through advanced photonics, signal processing, and data-driven intelligence.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW138383326 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;">We are expanding our R&amp;D team with an Integration Software Engineer who is passionate about quality, structured validation, and delivering robust software in complex engineering environments.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW17873096 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW17873096 BCX8">As a Software Test Engineer, you will be responsible for defining and executing practical software tests to validate software components (including algorithms, cloud back-end, and user interfaces) that process sensor signals generated by fiber-optic sensing systems. You will work closely with data scientists, signal processing specialists, back-end developers, and software architects to ensure that products meet functional and non-functional requirements.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW17873096 BCX8">This role requires a hands-on professional with a proactive mindset, a structured approach to software testing, strong attention to detail, and the ability to understand complex technical systems and translate requirements into effective test strategies.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW57822337 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h4><ul><li><p>Lead software integration engineering for our underwater acoustic sensing systems, ensuring frontend and backend components, algorithms, and hardware systems work together reliably.</p></li><li><p>Integrate the algorithmic toolbox with our system backends, turning research code into maintainable, versioned and deployable software components.</p></li><li><p>Implement data interfaces for our real-time sonar processing pipeline, to ingest multiple sensors (acoustic, heading, temperature, pressure, etc.) from internal and external data acquisition systems. Implement health reporting, logging and monitoring, so that the status and performance of software and system components is visible and actionable.</p></li><li><p>Develop the software control layer for our sensing systems and their hardware components, including APIs for commanding, state handling, error handling and recovery.</p></li><li><p>Implement, align and verify software integrations with external partners and C2 systems, being directly involved in defining interfaces, maintaining interface specifications and running joint integration tests.</p></li><li><p>Testing &amp; debugging: Develop system-level test suites and CI/CD pipelines, diagnose communication failures, and ensure secure, reliable data transfers as the toolbox and backends evolve.</p></li><li><p>Address performance, latency and scalability of the integrated pipeline, together with algorithm and backend developers.</p></li><li><p>Work hands-on with integrated software and hardware systems at our headquarters and production facility, with occasional on-site visits.</p></li><li><p>Review the work of junior engineers and external development partners in depth, promote good practices for packaging, versioning and release, and share integration knowledge across the team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">Why Join Us?</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p>Join one of Europe’s most promising deep-tech scale-ups.</p></li><li><p>Shape the future of a rapidly growing multidisciplinary R&amp;D organization.</p></li><li><p>Competitive salary and benefits package.</p></li><li><p>Enjoy regular team activities and company events.</p></li><li><p>Fresh team lunches provided 3 times/week.</p></li></ul> <br> <h4>Qualifications:</h4><ul><li><p>BSc or MSc in Computer Science, Software Engineering or a related field.</p></li><li><p>Significant professional experience in software engineering, with a focus on system integration, backend or platform development.</p></li><li><p>Extensive experience developing production software in Python, including packaging, testing, dependency management and writing maintainable, well-structured code.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with systems programming in C++, or Rust, for the purpose of extending Python for more performance or hardware control.</p></li><li><p>Proven experience designing and implementing APIs and messaging interfaces (e.g. MQTT, WebSocket) and data serialization (e.g. protobuf).</p></li><li><p>Experience with realtime data pipelines, and handling high-throughput or streaming data.</p></li><li><p>Experience with Docker, CI/CD and automated testing in a Linux environment.</p></li><li><p>Experience working with software that interacts with physical systems, and comfort doing hands-on integration and troubleshooting in a lab or production environment.</p></li><li><p>Experience reviewing code and designs, mentoring junior engineers, and setting engineering standards.</p></li><li><p>An outcome-focused mindset, with the ability to own a problem end to end or break it down for others.</p></li><li><p>Ability to work with algorithm developers and translate research code into robust, maintainable software.</p></li><li><p>Flexible and proactive in taking on what needs to be addressed, and comfortable in a fast-paced scale-up environment.</p></li><li><p>Good communication skills in English and the ability to coordinate with internal teams and external partners.</p></li><li><p>Willingness to work primarily from our Amsterdam headquarters, as parts of the role involve classified information and physical systems.</p></li></ul><h4></h4><h4>Nice to Have:</h4><ul><li><p>Knowledge of defense systems or defense standards (e.g. NATO STANAGs, MIL-STD), for example in naval, maritime security or surveillance systems.</p></li><li><p>Experience with the scientific Python stack (e.g. NumPy, SciPy) or integrating signal processing or ML models into production systems.</p></li><li><p>Experience developing software interfaces for controlling instruments or devices.</p></li><li><p>Experience with other messaging or streaming frameworks (e.g. Kafka, ZeroMQ, DDS).</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with observability tooling.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW236113144 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW236113144 BCX8"><strong>Security &amp; Compliance:</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW236113144 BCX8">You'll be working with clients in the defense and security sectors, obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD (Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service) is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. For more information, please refer to details on security screening.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/senior-integration-software-engineer-amsterdam-441860","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1794346279},{"slug":"senior-ai-ml-engineer-amsterdam-66773","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior AI/ML Engineer","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">We are looking for an experienced <strong>AI/ML Engineer</strong> to develop and deploy machine learning solutions for real-world underwater acoustic sensing systems.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW186153117 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW186153117 BCX8">Optics11 is a deep-tech company developing cutting-edge fiber-optic sensing technologies for challenging environments, including underwater acoustics, offshore energy, and defense applications. Our systems enable high-performance sensing and monitoring through advanced photonics, signal processing, and data-driven intelligence.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW186153117 BCX8">We are expanding our R&amp;D team with a Senior AI/ML Engineer who combines strong mathematical foundations with applied machine learning expertise to enhance the next generation of intelligent acoustic sensing solutions.</p><figure class="Paragraph SCXW186153117 BCX8"><img alt="Shape" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAAAXNSR0IArs4c6QAAAARnQU1BAACxjwv8YQUAAAAJcEhZcwAADsMAAA7DAcdvqGQAAAANSURBVBhXY2BgYGAAAAAFAAGKM+MAAAAAAElFTkSuQmCC"></figure><p class="Paragraph SCXW186153117 BCX8"><strong>Role Overview:</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW186153117 BCX8">As a Senior AI/ML Engineer, you will apply machine learning to real-world underwater acoustic sensing challenges using Optics11’s fiber-optic technology platforms. You will work closely with acoustics engineers, signal-processing specialists, and embedded/software teams to develop robust ML components that integrate seamlessly into operational systems.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW186153117 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW186153117 BCX8">This role requires a strong foundation in signal processing, applied mathematics, and statistics, and the ability to combine physics-based acoustic algorithms with data-driven ML methods.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Develop and implement machine learning solutions for underwater acoustic sensing use cases, including detection, classification, localization and anomaly monitoring within fiber-optic sensing systems.</p></li><li><p>Select and adapt modelling approaches based on data availability, operational constraints and system requirements.</p></li><li><p>Apply strong foundations in applied mathematics, statistics and signal processing (e.g., beamforming, spectral analysis, detection pipelines) and integrate these with modern data-driven ML techniques.</p></li><li><p>Design, train, evaluate and benchmark AI/ML models, ensuring robustness, generalization and deployment readiness.</p></li><li><p>Validate models rigorously across laboratory experiments and offshore field datasets, with clear performance tracking and reproducible experimentation.</p></li><li><p>Analyze and interpret large-scale experimental and real-world fiber-optic sensing datasets, contributing to scalable workflows for data preparation, labelling and augmentation.</p></li><li><p>Support technical trade-offs between accuracy, interpretability, latency and real-time or embedded constraints.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate closely with acoustics engineers, signal processing specialists, software and embedded teams to integrate ML components into operational acoustic sensing pipelines.</p></li><li><p>Translate complex AI/ML results into clear technical insights that inform system-level engineering decisions.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to strong engineering practices, including version-controlled experiments, documentation, traceability, validation standards and continuous improvement of ML components.</p></li><li><p>Stay informed about advances in AI/ML for time-series analysis, sensor fusion and signal-informed learning, and prototype promising approaches that complement the broader technology stack.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What's in it for you?</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Competitive salary .</p></li><li><p>Innovative high-tech, international organization .</p></li><li><p>The opportunity to work in a cross-functional and interdisciplinary environment .</p></li><li><p>A lot to learn and to develop, we stimulate personal development .</p></li><li><p>Lunches.</p></li></ul> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong><span style="background-color:#C6C6C6">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">MSc in Machine Learning, Signal Processing, Applied Mathematics, Computer Science, Physics, or a related field.<span style="background-color:#C6C6C6">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Strong foundation in linear algebra, probability, statistics, and signal processing.<span style="background-color:#C6C6C6">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p>Proven experience applying AI/ML methods to time-series or sensor data, including techniques such as:                         Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs), Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) (e.g., LSTMs),  Transformer-based architectures for time-series learning.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle2 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Supervised and unsupervised learning approaches for detection and classification.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Hands-on experience with model training, evaluation, and validation in applied settings.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Proficiency in Python and modern ML frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX).</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Ability to work in an applied R&amp;D environment with experimental and field data, balancing model performance with real-world constraints.</p></li></ul><figure class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8"><img alt="Shape" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAAAXNSR0IArs4c6QAAAARnQU1BAACxjwv8YQUAAAAJcEhZcwAADsMAAA7DAcdvqGQAAAANSURBVBhXY2BgYGAAAAAFAAGKM+MAAAAAAElFTkSuQmCC"></figure><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Experience with underwater acoustics, sonar, or beamforming-related applications.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Knowledge of embedded or real-time deployment constraints.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Experience with sensor fusion, self-supervised learning, or physics-informed ML.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Familiarity with offshore, defense, or industrial monitoring domains.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW158482370 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW158482370 BCX8">Familiarity with structured ML development processes such as CRISP-ML(Q) or similar lifecycle and quality frameworks.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">You'll be working with clients in the defense and security sectors, obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD (Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service) is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. For more information, please refer to details on security screening.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/senior-ai-ml-engineer-amsterdam-66773","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1794346279},{"slug":"senior-customer-solutions-engineer-netherlands-57373","company_name":"Plume","title":"Senior Customer Solutions Engineer","description":"<div class="content-intro"><p><strong>Life at Plume</strong></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">At Plume, we believe that technology isn't about moving faster, it's about making life's moments better. Which is why we've built the world's first, and only, open and hardware-independent service delivery platform for smart homes, small businesses, enterprises, and beyond. Our SaaS platform uses WiFi, advanced AI, and machine learning to create the future of connected spaces—and human experiences—at massive scale.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We now deliver services to over 60 million locations globally and have managed over 3 billion devices on our platform. We're expanding rapidly, pioneering a new category, and we achieved our Series F funding in just four years. Our customers include many of the world's largest Internet Service Providers (ISPs) who look to Plume to help them evolve their smart home offerings while gleaning insights from their own data.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">With a bias for action and a love for being trailblazers, the team at Plume embodies a combination of relentless curiosity and imaginative innovation. We challenge ourselves to think in ways that other companies don't, work to do what should be done (rather than what can), and if we can't do it exceptionally well, we don't do it. It's how we've assembled a team of world-class builders, thinkers, and doers. And it's how we're reinventing what's possible every day.</span></p></div><div>Plume is seeking an experienced and highly motivated&nbsp;<strong>Senior Customer Solutions Engineer</strong> to join our dynamic team. As a key technical advisor, you'll work directly with Internet Service Providers (ISPs), acting as the bridge between their business needs and our cutting-edge solutions. You'll play a crucial role in the sales process, from initial discovery to successful deployment, ensuring our partners achieve maximum value from our products.<br>This is a fantastic opportunity for a technically adept individual with a passion for networking, cloud, and AI who thrives in a customer-facing role.<br><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong><br>Responsibilities</strong></span></div>
<ul>
<li>Technical Trusted Advisor: Engage with ISPs to deeply understand their technical and business requirements, and then effectively demonstrate how Plume's solutions can meet and exceed those needs.</li>
<li>Product Demos &amp; Trials: Conduct compelling product demonstrations and manage complex proof-of-concept (PoC) and field trials, showcasing the tangible benefits of Plume's technology.</li>
<li>System Integration: Collaborate with our internal Customer Engineering, Product Management, and Operational teams to understand and deliver Plume's solutions within a customer's ecosystem. You'll work to integrate our solutions into their existing BSS/OSS, CRM, ticketing, and AI platforms using APIs and other integration methods.</li>
<li>Sales Enablement: Work closely with the sales organization to drive revenue, achieve sales quotas, and contribute to the overall growth of the business.</li>
<li>Presentations &amp; Events: Prepare and deliver high-impact presentations, including Quarterly Business Reviews (QBRs), and represent Plume at industry events and conferences.</li>
<li>Product Development Input: Provide valuable feedback to our product and engineering teams based on customer requirements and market trends, helping to inform the development of new features and solutions.</li>
<li>Technical Support: Offer prompt local and remote technical support for PoCs, lab trials, and deployment ramp-ups, ensuring a smooth and successful customer journey.</li>
<li>Industry Expertise: Continuously research and stay up-to-date on the latest industry standards and emerging technologies in networking, cloud architectures, and AI.</li>
</ul>
<div><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Experience &amp; Qualifications</strong></span></div>
<ul>
<li>Hands-on Technical Experience: Strong hands-on experience in the configuration and deployment of software and hardware, including Wi-Fi, networking equipment, and cloud services. A fundamental understanding of cloud architectures and AI principles is essential. Deep understanding and knowledge of Residential and SMB Gateways is a big plus.</li>
<li>ISP SaaS Experience: Proven experience working with ISPs to deploy large-scale SaaS network solutions to millions of endpoints.</li>
<li>Communication &amp; Collaboration: A track record of developing and maintaining professional, cooperative relationships with all levels of staff and customers.</li>
<li>Networking &amp; Cloud Certifications: Relevant certifications such as CWNA, CCNA, or AWS Solutions Architect are highly preferred.</li>
<li>Problem-Solving: Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to troubleshoot complex technical issues in a fast-paced environment.</li>
</ul>
<div><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Qualification Requirements</strong></span></div>
<ul>
<li>Experience: 5+ years of related experience working with network, security, SaaS, and/or AI industries.</li>
<li>Education: A BS/BA degree in a relevant field or equivalent work experience.</li>
<li>Industry Knowledge: In-depth industry knowledge and a strong understanding of SDN and wireless technologies, solutions, and product offerings are preferred.</li>
<li>Communication Skills: Advanced written and oral communication skills.</li>
<li>Travel: Ability to travel &gt;70% of the time.</li>
</ul>
<div><strong>Location/Language:</strong> <strong>This is a remote position. Candidates must be based in United Kingdom or Netherlands and be fluent in English.</strong></div><div class="content-conclusion"><p><strong>About Plume</strong></p>
