rm for conversational growth, with AI skills shaping how we build, how we work, and how we grow.</p><h2>WHO WE'RE LOOKING FOR 🌟</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your decisions here won't get lost in a big system. They'll define it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Staff Backend Engineer for Manychat for Brands, you’ll own the technical side of a new product. You’ll set the architecture and technical priorities with the team, and decide what lives in our Python services and what stays in the PHP-based Manychat platform. It’s an individual contributor role with a lot of room to make an impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The product fills a real gap. Brands pay influencers to post but then can’t see what happens next. We’re building the first view that shows it: who asked for the link, who opened the DM, who clicked, for every campaign, creator and post.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work with Product as a partner and stay close to brands and creators, so feedback reaches you fast and helps you shape Manychat for Brands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound like you? Let’s talk!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>YOUR FUTURE TEAMMATES 👋</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet the Engineering team:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We keep Manychat running smoothly under high load every single day and make sure it's ready to scale even further. We do it by combining strong engineering foundations with AI tools that let us move faster without cutting corners. And we're the ones who shape and own what gets built. AI accelerates. Humans own the thinking.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHAT YOU'LL DO 🚀</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the architecture and technical priorities for Brands together with the Engineering Manager and the team: service boundaries, data models, authentication, access control, and integration with the core Manychat platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide which logic belongs in the Python-based Brands services and which stays in the PHP-based Manychat platform. Think about data ownership, reliability, and long-term maintenance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead big system-level changes when the path isn't clear yet. Explore options, split the work into measurable milestones, and plan data migrations, gradual rollouts, and rollbacks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define reliability and performance requirements for key Brands workflows. Set metrics and observability, and check the impact of your changes on production data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find the root causes of slowdowns and repeated incidents across service boundaries, using metrics, logs, and distributed tracing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Security, Infrastructure, and Platform teams on solutions. Decide what to fix in the application and what needs other teams, and explain the trade-offs clearly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Product on the approach and scope of solutions, and suggest simpler options when you see them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make technical decisions easy to follow: document key choices and the reasons behind them, do thorough design and code reviews, and share your knowledge in complex areas.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>TO SHINE IN THIS ROLE 💥</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You'll need:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in Python backend development and a broad view of backend architecture beyond one language. You can understand existing systems, even when the technology is new to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong product mindset. You work closely with Product Managers, challenge assumptions, and explain technical trade-offs in terms of user experience, timelines, and product capabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning the 