ities around defined ICPs, customer problems, and commercial value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and coordinate launches across Product, Sales, Marketing, and CS—from readiness and evidence to external comms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build field-tested enablement materials (one-pagers, pitch decks, demo narratives, battle cards, and objection-handling guides) based on real sales conversations, not theory.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer &amp; Market Intelligence</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join sales calls, discovery sessions, and CS check-ins to spot recurring objections, use cases, and buying triggers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather competitive intelligence and market trends to inform product, pricing, and messaging decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Push back constructively when internal assumptions don't match market reality.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Release Governance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish a lightweight release process that separates early experiments from market-ready features and approved external claims.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Who we’re looking for</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for someone who talks about what they shipped, not what they planned. Someone structured, with good judgement and the confidence to tell us when something isn’t ready to sell.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 4–5 years of marketing experience, with at least 2–3 years directly in product marketing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a proven track record of creating or repositioning propositions, launches, and sales enablement materials that teams can execute without a walkthrough—and the outcomes to show for it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take strong project 