&lt;h3&gt;In return, this is what we offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get access to an international network of clients, colleagues, technology partners and resources. We have a listening ear for ambitious ideas, and together we keep stretching our boundaries. We want you to follow the path you’re building, and we invest in your personal development in a dynamic, collaborative workplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A monthly salary between &lt;strong&gt;€4,800 and €5200&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;gross, depending on your experience, seniority and fit with the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A gross annual 8% holiday allowance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to our commuting package to suit your individual needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pension benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A choice of a Mac or Windows laptop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A culture of trust, with a feel-at-home vibe and an international environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health support, including complimentary membership EAP counselling services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefits (when available) including yoga classes, an in-house masseuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to work with a renowned international customer base of B2B and B2C brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence and world-class partnerships – all united by our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open – we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://wpp.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;normaltextrun&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;WPP (VML/WPP Enterprise Solutions) is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;scxw176048299&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you click &quot;Submit Application&quot;, this will send any information you add below to WPP (VML/WPP Enterprise Solutions). Before you do this, we think it&#39;s a good idea to read through our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vml.com/recruitment-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;. California residents should read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vml.com/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. This explains what we do with your personal data when you apply for a role with us, and, how you can update the information you have provided us with or how to remove it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vmlenterprisesolutions/business-analyst-enterprise-ai-solutions-amsterdam-361566","tags":["Technology & Innovation"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794315320},{"slug":"senior-product-marketing-manager-zaltbommel-103725","company_name":"Cyclomedia Technology","title":"(Senior) Product Marketing Manager (d/f/m)","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Location:</strong> Zaltbommel, Netherlands (Hybrid)</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Reporting to:</strong> VP of Marketing</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><span style="background-color:#C6C6C6"><br></span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>About Cyclomedia &amp; The Role<br><br></strong>Cyclomedia creates digital representations of the real world, giving professionals the visual data they need to manage assets and infrastructure. We are currently sharpening our commercial strategy. To drive this, we are looking for a Product Marketing Manager to bridge the gap between our product capabilities and the market.<br><span style="background-color:#C6C6C6"><br></span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0">In our setup, Product Management builds the solution, and Product Marketing wins the market. As part of the Marketing department, you keep our messaging strictly focused on customer value. You own the value propositions, the customer context, and the commercial message. Your output forms the foundation for all our demand generation campaigns.<br><br></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>The Role &amp; Collaboration</strong> <br><br>As the owner of our value propositions, you define the go-to-market approach. You build this strategy through direct contact with customers and close alignment with sales and Product Management. Armed with this market reality, you brief our Regional Marketing Managers and Content Marketers on the target audiences, messaging, and commercial hooks required for their campaigns. You also work with our Sales Enablement team to ensure sales representatives have the materials they need to close deals.<br><span style="background-color:#C6C6C6"><br></span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong><span style="background-color:#C6C6C6"><br></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Positioning &amp; Messaging:</strong> Translate technical product capabilities into clear positioning and go-to-market strategies that drive pipeline value and improve lead conversion rates.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Market Intelligence:</strong> Feed the product roadmap with market insights, buyer needs, and competitive intelligence.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Sales Alignment:</strong> Validate marketing materials with regional sales teams so they are fully equipped to sell the solution.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>First 6 Months Impact:</strong> Work out the context for our top 6 value propositions and produce the foundational global marketing materials to guide upcoming demand and lead generation campaigns.<br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Your Profile</strong><span style="background-color:#C6C6C6"><br></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Experience:</strong> 5+ years of Product Marketing experience, or a strong commercial background deeply embedded in our core markets.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Domain Expertise (Preferred):</strong> A background in Geographic Information Systems (GIS) or mobile mapping, or specific industry experience in utility companies, telecom network planning, public or network asset management, or engineering work planning.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Commercial Acumen:</strong> A proven ability to look from the outside in. You base your strategies on what the buyer needs to hear rather than what the product can do.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Ownership:</strong> You work independently and possess the maturity to help shape the Product Marketing function as we grow.<span style="background-color:#C6C6C6"><br></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>What We Offer</strong><span style="background-color:#C6C6C6"><br></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Room to make your mark:</strong> A challenging role in a strong, growing international company, with real freedom to shape the position.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>A great team to join:</strong> A small, close-knit and growing marketing team, plus experienced colleagues to build on.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>A competitive package:</strong> An attractive base salary and an 8.3% annual bonus scheme.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Growth:</strong> Training, online courses and (team) coaching to support your development.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Time off:</strong> 25 holidays, the option to buy up to 10 extra days a year, and an extra day off after Ascension Day.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Wellbeing:</strong> A flexible Mental Health Day each year to rest and recharge, and a sports allowance of €25 gross per month.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>Hybrid working:</strong> 3 days in the office and 2 from home, with a home-working allowance of €2 per day.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW177615231 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW177615231 BCX0"><strong>The right tools:</strong> A company phone and laptop.</p></li></ul> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/cyclomedia-technology/senior-product-marketing-manager-zaltbommel-103725","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Zaltbommel, Gelderland, Netherlands","created_at":1794313884},{"slug":"net-developer-ridderkerk-91680","company_name":"Verzuimdata B.V.","title":".NET Developer","description":"<h2>Wat je gaat doen als .NET Developer</h2><p>Bij Verzuimdata B.V. in Ridderkerk bouw en onderhoud je software die de gegevensuitwisseling rondom verzuim, loon en werknemers beheert tussen werkgevers, verzekeraars, arbodiensten en de overheid. Je werkt aan onze portals en ondersteunende oplossingen voor polisbeheer, premie- en schadeberekening, en dashboards.</p><h2>Wat we van je vragen</h2><p>Je hebt gedegen ervaring met .NET en softwareontwikkeling binnen een vergelijkbare rol. Je kunt zelfstandig werken en schakelt gemakkelijk binnen ons team van 11-50 medewerkers om processen rondom gegevensuitwisseling te optimaliseren.</p><h2>Arbeidsvoorwaarden</h2><ul><li><p>Je ontvangt een salaris van EUR 3,000–3,500 per month.</p></li><li><p>Je krijgt extra vakantiedagen bovenop je 20 vakantiedagen per jaar, flexibele werktijden en doorbetaald ziekteverlof.</p></li><li><p>Je profiteert van een reiskostenvergoeding, gratis parkeren en een laptop van de zaak.</p></li><li><p>Je beschikt over een thuiswerkuitrusting en de mogelijkheid om thuis te werken.</p></li><li><p>Je geniet op kantoor van gratis drankjes en een gratis lunch.</p></li></ul><h2>Jouw eerste maanden bij Verzuimdata B.V.</h2><p>In je eerste maanden maak je kennis met onze systemen en ons team op locatie in Ridderkerk. Je pakt direct taken op rondom onze software en draagt bij aan het eenvoudig en foutloos maken van gegevensstromen. Mocht je niet aan elk gevraagd punt voldoen, dan nodigen we je toch uit om te reageren.</p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/verzuimdata-bv/net-developer-ridderkerk-91680","tags":["Software Development"],"job_types":["Vast contract","professional / ervaren"],"location":"Ridderkerk","created_at":1794310259},{"slug":"junior-systeembeheerder-ridderkerk-418551","company_name":"Verzuimdata B.V.","title":"Junior systeembeheerder","description":"<h2>Ben jij iemand die graag de handen uit de mouwen steekt, energie krijgt van techniek en het leuk vindt om collega's verder te helpen? Krijg je een kick van het oplossen van IT-uitdagingen en vind je het interessant om een moderne IT-omgeving draaiende én up-to-date te houden? Dan zijn wij op zoek naar jou! Voor ons IT-team zoeken we een enthousiaste en gedreven junior systeembeheerder die niet alleen zorgt dat alles werkt, maar ook graag meedenkt over hoe het nóg beter, slimmer en veiliger kan. Lijkt het je interessant om te werken met een moderne Microsoft-omgeving én mee te bouwen aan een van de eerste Nederlandse implementaties van HPE Morpheus VM Essentials? Dan hebben we een mooie uitdaging voor je!</h2><h2>Wat je gaat doen</h2><p>Als junior systeembeheerder in Ridderkerk beheer en ondersteun je de IT-infrastructuur op locatie binnen een team van 11-50 medewerkers. Je werkt 40 uur per week op basis van een vast contract met een proeftijd van 1 maand.</p><h2>Arbeidsvoorwaarden</h2><ul><li><p>Extra vakantiedagen bovenop de 20 vakantiedagen per jaar.</p></li><li><p>Flexibele werktijden om je werk en planning af te stemmen.</p></li><li><p>Gratis drankjes en gratis lunch op de locatie in Ridderkerk.</p></li><li><p>Gratis parkeren bij het kantoor.</p></li><li><p>Een laptop van de zaak en een complete thuiswerkuitrusting inclusief de optie om thuis te werken.</p></li><li><p>Reiskostenvergoeding voor je woon-werkverkeer.</p></li></ul><h2>Salaris</h2><p>Het salaris bedraagt EUR 2,750–2,950 per month.</p><h2>Jouw eerste maanden bij Verzuimdata</h2><p>Je maakt kennis met de systemen en de infrastructuur van Verzuimdata in Ridderkerk. Heb je niet op elk vlak direct de volledige ervaring, maar herken je jezelf in de rol? Reageer dan gerust.</p><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/verzuimdata-bv/junior-systeembeheerder-ridderkerk-418551","tags":["System and Network Administration"],"job_types":["Vast contract","instapniveau"],"location":"Ridderkerk","created_at":1794310259},{"slug":"power-bi-developer-ridderkerk-367762","company_name":"Verzuimdata B.V.","title":"Power BI Developer","description":"<h2>Ben jij analytisch, klantgericht en heb je een passie voor data? Bij Verzuimdata zijn wij op zoek naar een Power BI Developer die ons helpt om data om te zetten in waardevolle inzichten. In deze rol werk je zowel zelfstandig als samen met collega's aan uitdagende BI-vraagstukken. Je hebt regelmatig contact met klanten, inventariseert wensen en vertaalt deze naar gebruiksvriendelijke dashboards en rapportages. Of je nu een ambitieuze starter bent of al wat meer ervaring hebt: wij bieden je de ruimte om jezelf verder te ontwikkelen binnen een groeiende en innovatieve omgeving.</h2><h2>Wat je gaat doen</h2><p>Als Power BI Developer ontwerp en beheer je diverse dashboards en zorg je dat data optimaal wordt ingezet voor de ondersteuning van de dagelijkse processen binnen de verzekerings- en verzuimbranche.</p><h2>Wat we vragen</h2><ul><li><p>Ervaring met Business Intelligence en Power BI</p></li><li><p>Zelfstandige en nauwkeurige werkhouding</p></li><li><p>Beschikbaarheid voor 40 uur per week</p></li></ul><h2>Arbeidsvoorwaarden</h2><ul><li><p>Je ontvangt een salaris van EUR 3,000–3,500 per month.</p></li><li><p>Je krijgt extra vakantiedagen en 20 vakantiedagen per jaar.</p></li><li><p>Je profiteert van flexibele werktijden en de mogelijkheid tot remote werken.</p></li><li><p>Er is een reiskostenvergoeding en gratis parkeren op locatie.</p></li><li><p>Je ontvangt een laptop van de zaak en thuiswerkuitrusting.</p></li><li><p>Er wordt doorbetaald ziekteverlof geregeld.</p></li><li><p>Je geniet van gratis drankjes en een gratis lunch op kantoor.</p></li></ul><h2>Jouw eerste maanden bij Verzuimdata</h2><p>In je eerste maanden maak je kennis met de systemen en de gegevensstromen tussen werkgevers, verzekeraars en arbodiensten. Je pakt direct de ontwikkeling en optimalisatie van dashboards op om de datastromen inzichtelijk te maken.</p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/verzuimdata-bv/power-bi-developer-ridderkerk-367762","tags":["Business Intelligence"],"job_types":["Vast contract","professional / ervaren"],"location":"Ridderkerk","created_at":1794310258},{"slug":"medewerker-service-support-ridderkerk-456165","company_name":"Verzuimdata B.V.","title":"Medewerker Service & Support","description":"<h2>Vind jij het leuk om samen met jouw team aan één doel te werken? Op onze Servicedesk, een dynamische omgeving, is geen dag hetzelfde. Hier leer je elke dag wat nieuws om het gezamenlijke doel, de klant zo correct mogelijk helpen, te bereiken. Ben jij iemand die klantgerichtheid voorop heeft staan, snel kan schakelen, zelfstandig kan werken, ondernemend is en graag initiatief neemt? Ga dan aan de slag als Medewerker Service & Support!</h2><h2>Wat je gaat doen</h2><p>Als Medewerker Service & Support help je klanten zo correct mogelijk op de servicedesk. Je schakelt snel, werkt zelfstandig en neemt initiatief om gegevensuitwisseling eenvoudig te laten verlopen.</p><h2>Wat wij vragen</h2><ul><li><p>Klantgerichtheid staat bij jou voorop.</p></li><li><p>Je kunt snel schakelen en zelfstandig werken.</p></li><li><p>Je bent ondernemend en neemt graag initiatief.</p></li></ul><h2>Wat je kunt verwachten</h2><p>Je bouwt pensioen op via de bedrijfspensioenregeling en krijgt extra vakantiedagen bovenop de 20 vakantiedagen per jaar. De werkweek kent flexibele werktijden en er is ruimte voor thuiswerken met een thuiswerkuitrusting en een vergoeding voor reiskosten of openbaar vervoer.</p><p>Op kantoor in Ridderkerk krijg je een gratis lunch, gratis drankjes en kun je gebruikmaken van gratis parkeren en een laptop van de zaak. Daarnaast worden bij ziekte de uren doorbetaald.</p><h2>Jouw eerste maanden bij Verzuimdata</h2><p>In je eerste maanden leer je de dagelijkse processen van onze servicedesk kennen en werk je samen met je team aan een correcte ondersteuning van onze gebruikers. Mocht je niet aan elk vereist punt voldoen, nodigen wij je toch uit om te reageren.</p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/verzuimdata-bv/medewerker-service-support-ridderkerk-456165","tags":["Customer Service"],"job_types":["Vast contract","instapniveau"],"location":"Ridderkerk","created_at":1794323853},{"slug":"ml-infrastructure-acceleration-engineer-llms-amsterdam-392610","company_name":"Prosus","title":"ML Infrastructure & Acceleration Engineer - LLMs","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><h2>Who we're looking for</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're seeking an experienced ML Infrastructure &amp; Acceleration Engineer to own the GPU infrastructure that powers our LLM training and serving, and to make every workload on it faster and cheaper. You'll run our H200 cluster end to end, deploy models to production, and profile and optimize our training and inference pipelines down to the kernel level when it matters. You understand GPUs from the cluster scheduler to the memory hierarchy, you measure before you optimize, and you're motivated by turning raw compute into faster iteration for our ML team. You thrive in environments where infrastructure reliability and efficiency directly shape how quickly research reaches millions of users.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>GPU Cluster &amp; Infrastructure:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own our H200 GPU cluster end to end: Kubernetes and Slurm for training and inference workloads, with multi-tenant scheduling, quotas, and resource isolation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep large distributed training runs healthy: node health checks, NCCL and interconnect debugging, automated job recovery, and checkpoint management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track and optimize GPU utilization and cost across training and inference, with dashboards and budget alerting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage infrastructure-as-code and provisioning for GPU environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and monitor SLIs/SLOs for cluster availability and production model serving</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deployment &amp; Serving:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deploy LLMs to production using vLLM or SGLang, with CI/CD, model versioning, and safe rollouts and rollbacks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor serving latency, throughput, errors, and cost, and act on regressions</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ML Acceleration:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Profile training and inference end to end (PyTorch Profiler, Nsight Systems, Nsight Compute) to find and remove bottlenecks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve training throughput and MFU: parallelism strategies (FSDP, tensor and pipeline parallelism), communication/compute overlap, mixed precision and FP8, activation checkpointing, torch.compile</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optimize inference: quantization (FP8, INT8, INT4), speculative decoding, prefix caching, continuous batching, KV cache tuning, and parallelism layouts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write or integrate fused and custom kernels (Triton, CUDA) where off-the-shelf implementations fall short</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build benchmarking tooling so every optimization ships with measured gains</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enablement &amp; Best Practices:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with ML engineers and researchers to make training and serving efficient by default</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish best practices for using the cluster and guide teams in their adoption</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Minimum qualifications</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in ML infrastructure, MLOps, HPC, or platform engineering with focus on GPU workloads</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience operating multi-node GPU clusters with Kubernetes and/or Slurm, including debugging hardware, networking (NCCL, InfiniBand/RoCE), and job failures</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Production experience deploying and optimizing LLM inference with vLLM, SGLang, or TensorRT-LLM</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of profiling and accelerating GPU workloads, with measured results in throughput, latency, MFU, or cost</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of monitoring and observability for GPU systems (Prometheus, Grafana, DCGM, or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Naturally curious with a track record of proactively identifying and implementing improvements</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Preferred qualifications</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing custom kernels in Triton or CUDA, and familiarity with fused kernels such as FlashAttention</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Performance tuning of distributed training frameworks: FSDP, Megatron-LM, or DeepSpeed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with low-precision training and inference (**FP8**, INT4) and model compression for production deployment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of GPU architectures: memory hierarchy, tensor cores, roofline analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with multi-tenant GPU scheduling and fair-share resource allocation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributions to open-source projects such as vLLM, SGLang, PyTorch, or Triton</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Critical infrastructure ownership for high-impact AI projects that are strategically vital to the company, with direct visibility to senior leadership including the CEO</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">State-of-the-art GPU infrastructure: H200 fleet, vLLM serving stack, and the freedom to optimize it end to end</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert ML team who have released top Hugging Face models, published at NeurIPS, and built production systems that will run on your infrastructure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant autonomy in choosing tools and shaping our infrastructure and performance strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Modern tooling: Latest ML frameworks, coding assistants, best-in-class development environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work model with our Amsterdam office - home to the AI House, bringing together 200+ AI professionals through events and collaborations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation, top-spec MacBook Pro, and an environment genuinely built for professional growth and learning</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited to own the GPU infrastructure behind cutting-edge LLMs and make every training run and every request faster, let's talk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/ml-infrastructure-acceleration-engineer-llms-amsterdam-392610","tags":["AI & ML"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794303619},{"slug":"ai-automation-intern-communications-amsterdam-283753","company_name":"Prosus","title":"AI Automation Intern, Communications","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Group Communications supports senior leadership and works across a wide network of portfolio companies, partners and AI initiatives. We want to get much better at using AI tools and data to track what is said about us, manage our relationships, and measure the value of our work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join the team as a hands-on AI intern. You will set up tools, build simple workflows and give the team the insight it needs to make decisions faster. It is a practical role with real ownership and direct exposure to senior leaders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help the Group Communications team use AI and data to work smarter: set up media monitoring, build a shared stakeholder CRM and track the metrics that show our impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Priority use cases</strong></h2><h3><strong>1. Media monitoring platform</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help assess, set up and configure a media monitoring platform, using AI for tagging, sentiment and summaries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the search terms, sources and alerts for the Group, key executives and priority topics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce regular media summaries and flag emerging issues or opportunities to the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test AI tools that make monitoring faster and more accurate, and recommend improvements.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>2. Stakeholder CRM: Ventures, Illuminate, AI House India, AI House Amsterdam</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and build a simple, shared CRM for contacts, partners, media and events across the four areas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consolidate existing contact lists, clean the data, and set clear rules for how the team keeps it current.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI to enrich records, log interactions and surface follow-ups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Train team members to use it and make sure it meets data privacy (GDPR) requirements.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>3. Metrics and data tracking</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agree a core set of communications KPIs with the team, for example reach, share of voice, sentiment, engagement and event outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a dashboard that pulls data from monitoring, social and CRM sources.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce monthly and quarterly reporting with clear insights for leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate data collection and reporting where possible to save the team time.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What success looks like</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First 3 months:</strong> media monitoring is live with regular summaries, and the CRM structure is agreed and populated.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>By the end of the internship:</strong> the team uses the CRM day to day, a KPI dashboard is in place, and there is clear handover documentation so the tools keep running.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A current student or recent graduate in communications, data, business, computer science or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude or Copilot and curiosity about how to apply them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Excel or Google Sheets skills and comfort working with data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured way of working, with the ability to turn messy information into clear systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written English and the confidence to work with senior stakeholders.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with a CRM (for example HubSpot, Salesforce or Airtable) or a media monitoring tool (for example Meltwater or Cision).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dashboarding skills in Power BI, Looker Studio or Tableau.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Basic automation or scripting, for example Zapier, Power Automate or Python.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/ai-automation-intern-communications-amsterdam-283753","tags":["Communications"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794303619},{"slug":"field-sales-account-executive-the-hague-268580","company_name":"Lightspeedhq","title":"Field Sales Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is driven by building the restaurant platform that helps restaurants adapt, take control, and get back to what they do best: building the businesses they love.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Field Account Executive, you will be part of a team that is transforming the way restaurants operate. Using a consultative approach, you will prospect, build relationships, and sign up new restaurateurs in your local area. By understanding their unique needs, you will develop a customised solution that helps their business thrive. We need your passion and sales expertise to help us build the Lightspeed brand in your area. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generate lists of prospective restaurants and manage the entire sales cycle from initial outbound call/ walk in to close (experience with self-sourcing clients is a huge plus)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct demos and develop a solution that best meets the prospect’s needs </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with teams across the business to ensure that expectations set during the sales process are met in delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage Salesforce (our CRM) to manage all sales activities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand the competitive landscape and determine how to best position Lightspeed in the market</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will bring to the team: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dutch fluency is a must </strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a sourcing or closing customers, restaurant operations, or a relatable field and industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since this is a field position, you will be out and about on a daily basis in your territory </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication, organisational and presentation skills with the ability to sell and negotiate at all decision-making levels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of success in meeting and exceeding goals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial and team environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-motivated, creative, and flexible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">General technical proficiency with software</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Salesforce CRM is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Come Live the Lightspeed Experience….</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine career growth opportunities based on performance within a company that's continuously expanding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Uncapped commission</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with highly skilled people who are as passionate about sales &amp; marketing as you are</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An environment that encourages initiatives and leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a team big enough for growth but lean enough to make a real impact;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>and enjoy a range of benefits that’ll keep you happy, healthy and (not) hungry:</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed equity scheme (we are all owners)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health &amp; Wellness Credit- expense up to 400 EUR per year towards your gym membership, yoga classes, a new bike or whatever else you do for your health </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental Health Support through the Modern Health App- whether it is meditation, coaching or counseling you need - each employee gets access to this platform </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People Experience - Our PX benefit allows you to work from pretty much anywhere in the world for 60 days a year </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">LinkedIn Learning: At Lightspeed we believe in having a growth mindset, we provide free access to LinkedIn learning along with your career GPS to help you learn &amp; grow</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Subsidy to annual travel pass if you travel by public transport to the office </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular breakfast or lunches, drinks &amp; snacks in our Amsterdam office </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To all recruitment agencies: Lightspeed does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. If we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy, Lightspeed will not be responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Lightspeed is a proud equal opportunity employer and we are committed to creating an inclusive and barrier-free workplace. Lightspeed welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where to from here?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obviously, this has to be mutually beneficial: we want you to step into a role you love, and we want to offer you a place you’re proud to come to every day. For a glimpse into our world check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/careers/">career page here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is building communities through commerce, and we need people from all backgrounds and lived experiences to do that. We were founded in 2005, in Montreal’s gay village and our original members were all part of the LGBTQ+ community. The ethos of our business has been about inclusion from the very beginning, and we strive to provide a workplace where everyone belongs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who we are:</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powering the businesses that are the backbone of the global economy, Lightspeed's one-stop commerce platform helps merchants innovate to simplify, scale, and provide exceptional customer experiences. Our cloud commerce solution transforms and unifies online and physical operations, multichannel sales, expansion to new locations, global payments, financial solutions, and connection to supplier networks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Montréal, Canada in 2005, Lightspeed is dual-listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: LSPD) and Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: LSPD). With teams across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific, the company serves retail, hospitality, and golf businesses in over 100 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed handles your information in